WEBVTT

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.620
That day, the Professor asked us to meet him,

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.020
and we climbed the hill
behind the housing complex.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.830
At the time, I couldn't understand why
the Professor, who was normally so stern,

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:45.400
would suddenly ask us to join him, or why
he suggested climbing the hill of all things.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.950
All I knew was that he
wasn't his usual strict self,

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:56.110
and I was kinda happy to hear him
invite us along in such a kind voice.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.250
That night was the first and last time
I saw such a kindhearted look

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.460
on our teacher's--on Prof. Dominic's face.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.160
Can you keep up, Renton?

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.910
Yeah, I'm okay.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:12.960
How about Eureka?

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.040
Hey, what's the holdup, Eureka?

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.850
Renton! Nirvash isn't following us!

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.310
Aw, not again... I can't believe that guy.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.870
What's the matter?! C'mon, Nirvash, hurry up!

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.830
Hey!

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.490
C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.080
--Nirvash!
- -Nirvash!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.580
What's the matter? Hurry up?!

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.540
Nirvash!

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:58.720
Renton!

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.220
Cut it out!

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.750
Uh-oh, Mom's gonna chew me out again.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.790
I swear, it's always your fault.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.730
He's all soft 'n squishy!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.160
Hey! Don't scare her like that!

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.540
What, really?

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.960
It's okay, Eureka.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.290
He said it tickles when
somebody pets him like that.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.670
Oh, you can understand
what he's saying, Renton.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:36.180
Hm? Yeah.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.200
You're pretty amazing, Renton.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.280
People can't normally understand
what larvae are saying.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.000
Maybe you really are the chosen one, Renton.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.230
What's the matter?

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:01.910
Eureka!

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.750
No, stop it! If Eureka is
hit by sunlight, she'll--

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.870
Don't worry.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.620
Artificial light won't harm Eureka's body.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.700
Really?

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.790
As long as it's not real
sunlight, she'll be fine.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.190
Professor, that ship is broken down.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.370
It's not broken, it's been attacked.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.330
Attacked?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.040
Yes. Right now, humanity is at war
with a mysterious enemy called the EIZO

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.030
that are invading the Earth.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.390
I don't see why we can't all be friends.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.870
If we were friends, then the war
would end. Right,

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:48.540
Professor?

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:05.660
Professor, what are you doing?

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.570
Found it! Here, take a look.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.690
Professor, what kind of plant is this?

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.940
It's not a plant. It's
called a snow moon flower.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.860
Snow moon flower?

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:26.250
--Right. Just before winter ends each year,
--Nirvash!

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.910
--they bloom, buried in the snow like this.
--Come look! There's a cute flower!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.400
I've never seen anything like this before.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.250
There's a legend that goes
along with this flower.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:37.540
A legend?

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:43.080
Once every hundred years, it's said
that on days when stardust falls,

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.500
snow moon flowers blossom and
shine with the light of a rainbow.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.540
Stardust? What's that?

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:52.370
Beats me. I have no idea
what it means, either.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:55.110
Wow, there are things that you don't know...

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.560
But I do know this much.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:03.570
If you make a wish inside its rainbow light,
that wish is sure to come true.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.500
You can wish for anything?

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.540
Yeah.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.040
Will it bloom today?

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.990
Maybe, maybe not.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.280
And you, Eureka? Is there anything
that you want to wish for?

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.700
He says that when this flower
shines like a rainbow,

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.950
whatever you wish for will come true!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.830
Um, well... There's a wish that I wanna make.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:25.910
Like what?

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:31.640
I hear all kinds of stories from Renton.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.410
Like how he saw birds flying in the sky.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:38.040
Or how he saw a butterfly
hatch from a cocoon!

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.700
Or how he caught a fish in the river!

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:43.820
Or about a huge rainbow
that he saw up in the sky!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.150
Lots and lots of things!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:49.330
And that's why I want to see
all those things for myself!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.830
I want to see them together with Renton!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.630
So that's why I wanna--

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:55.790
Professor, look! The flower!

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.280
It's so pretty!

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.380
Look, its seeds are...

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:16.890
What happened to the flower?

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:21.560
Should've known; it didn't work...

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.330
Professor, what was that just now?

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:25.450
What about the flower?

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.870
It died.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.370
Let's look around and see
if there are more flowers!

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.700
No, it doesn't matter.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.870
Here. You two can have these.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:39.330
Its seeds?

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.480
They shouldn't go to waste.
You should use them as good-luck charms.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.450
Would you do me one favor?

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:50.300
What is it?

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:54.340
I have to go off and work on an experiment.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.290
Would you take my place and
watch over this hill for me?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.940
I want you to watch over this hill
where the snow moon flower blooms.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.660
And one day, work together and see to it

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.290
that a flower blooms here with
all the colors of the rainbow.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.290
I'm counting on you.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:15.940
The next morning, the Professor left
town without even saying goodbye.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:21.170
It was a week later that
we learned that he'd died.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:22.790
"Massive Explosion at Military Facility
50,000 Dead"

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.450
I don't know any of the details,
but even as young as I was,
"Massive Explosion at Military Facility
50,000 Dead"

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.500
I don't know any of the details,
but even as young as I was,

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.910
I knew that the Professor had died
in one of my father's experiments

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:35.840
to find a way to defeat the invading EIZO,
mankind's mortal enemy.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.060
And then...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.890
"Compulsory Search of Warsaw Labs"
...that fateful day arrived.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:51.150
As the representative of the
government, the Liberation Army

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.320
will hereby conduct a compulsory search
of the Warsaw Laboratories, and...

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.870
I'm scared, Renton...

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:01.450
It's okay. The people here
aren't doing anything wrong.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:06.040
Mom and Dad told me that the Warsaw
Labs were conducting important research

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.700
that would save humanity.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.000
But I'm still scared...

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.200
Everything will be okay.
I know these will protect us.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:14.930
--They will?
- -Yep.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.160
The seeds that the Professor gave us.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:20.970
That's why I know it'll be okay.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.750
Subject located!

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:27.340
Capture her!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.530
You little--

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:34.550
Nirvash!

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.290
No!

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.580
Eureka!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.870
Let go! Let go of her!

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:48.660
--No! Let me go!
--Expose the subject to sunlight to verify!

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.000
--Renton!
- -No, don't!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.500
Don't let the light hit Eureka!

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.930
Help me! Renton, help me!

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:03.830
--It hurts! It hurts, Renton! Help me!
--Confirmed! Return to base at once!

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.120
Help me!

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.020
No matter how much my head
ordered my body to move, it refused.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.150
--Eureka begged and pleaded for help,
--Help me, Renton...

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.530
but I was so scared that I
didn't lift so much as a finger.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.910
That was the moment when I first learned

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.180
I didn't have the means or the courage

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.160
to protect the things
that were precious to me.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.040
This is the assault carrier Gekko,

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:49.400
attached to the Liberation Army's
1st Division, 303rd Desperation Regiment.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.820
This is Captain Talho Yuki,
addressing all personnel.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:56.250
Our mission is the retrieval of a
top secret item that was left behind

00:09:56.250 --> 00:10:00.780
at the South Dakota military base that
is currently under attack from the EIZO.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:05.040
All KLF strike units will work
in unison and infiltrate the base.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.040
Get in there and secure that item!

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.240
EIZO are currently advancing southwards

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.240
towards central South Dakota at 51 knots.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.670
Estimated time to fusion: 600 seconds!

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.760
Got that? We're on a deadline here.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.750
Drive everything from your heads
but retrieving the top-secret item!

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:24.280
This is the first step in the plan
that we absolutely must carry out.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:28.200
--What is it?
--Dial it down, Talho.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.560
Holland...

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:32.070
You fainted yesterday, remember?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.070
Don't push yourself so hard.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:40.370
But this operation is the first step
towards our--no, <i>your </i>dream.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.830
You're right. And that's
exactly why you shouldn't...

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.410
...push yourself too hard here.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.540
Don't you try anything crazy either, Holland.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:51.290
Nirvash lockdown confirmed. Deploy catapult.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:56.110
It'll be okay... Just do it like in
the simulations and you'll be okay.

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:57.830
--Time delay, 17 seconds.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:00.710
--Hurry through the checklist!
--You did fine in the mock drills, right?

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:07.290
Yeah, you're right... If anybody can
come through this in one piece, it's us.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:13.410
The Gekko has just breached line 5-5-7.
We have visual confirmation of the EIZO.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.570
Those are humanity's mortal enemy...?

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:17.790
--Those are the invaders?
--CV/GATE synch confirmed.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:19.700
--Those are the EIZO?
--Course is clear!

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.040
Nirvash is go for launch!

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:26.620
This is Corporal Renton Thurston.
Nirvash is away!

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.250
April, 2009 AD.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:44.800
Mysterious gigantic lifeforms
that came to be called the EIZO

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.830
suddenly appeared in the South Pacific
and began an invasion of Earth.

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:54.040
A war between EIZO and humanity began,
and has raged for 45 years.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:00.830
The explosive speed of the EIZO
invasion could not be curbed,

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:04.660
and it was believed that humanity's
extinction was only a matter of time.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.690
It is now the year 2054.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:12.430
The People's Central Government
decided to use the

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:14.730
"Hammer of God," a doomsday
weapon employing solar energy,

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:17.220
to burn the EIZO to ashes.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.210
A plan was set in motion to
eliminate opposing factions

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:24.660
and to build the Megaroad, a colony ship
which would carry a select 20,000 people

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:31.120
to escape the coming deadly winter
of ash that would envelop the Earth.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:37.150
But a turn of events that the government
could not have predicted began to unfold.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:46.330
Why, yes, it works quite well
as an introduction to the story.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:52.450
However, there might not be
enough time to give it an ending.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.830
I believe that I've made all
the necessary preparations,

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.700
but there isn't much time, Dominic.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:02.960
Even so, I intend to keep my word.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:06.660
After all, your students are on their way.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.620
The children that you entrusted
all your hopes to are coming here.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.220
"State Parliament Building Plaza"

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.550
Masao!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.330
Masao, get up!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.690
Hurry, run away!

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:05.770
There was a military port 5 km to
the east! You should be safe there!

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:15.330
What was that?

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:20.400
The Devilfish? But that means...
Commander Holland?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:23.790
Holy crap, these things are strong...

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:26.990
Got no choice, then...
Compac Feedback System, activate!

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:34.340
Where is it? Where's your soul?

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:40.540
What's this feeling...? My heart, it's...

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:49.740
Where is it? Where are
you keeping your soul?!

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.950
Got it!

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.000
<i>That's</i> where it is!

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:03.950
Oh, wow...

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.890
What are you doing, rookie?

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:10.910
We're not here on a rescue mission.
Our job is to retrieve that top-secret item.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.930
--But I...
- -No buts!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:16.720
If this operation doesn't succeed,
it's the end of the road for us.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.520
We don't have time to save
the lives of strangers!

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.630
If you want to live, you have to accept that.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.490
I'm going on ahead.

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:30.010
Commander...

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.030
I have to survive...

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.040
I have to survive, no matter what.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.950
Okay, let's do this, Nirvash!

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:43.920
Huh?

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:48.160
Hey, what's the matter, Nirvash?
Hurry up and move!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.200
What do you mean, "Mukyuu"?

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.010
You found her?
What do you mean?

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.380
Found who?

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:01.440
Message from the flagship Shinano!
EIZO advance accelerating!

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:04.230
They will cross the alert line in...
They've crossed it!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.580
What's the time delay?

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:06.870
Plus 1-4-6!

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:08.520
Have we made contact with the target?

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:09.490
Not yet!

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:14.370
This is the Gekko. Holland, the EIZO are
advancing even faster than expected.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.740
At this rate, they'll get the drop on us!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.370
I know, I know! There's just
too many of these monsters!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.790
What the--? What the hell was that?

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.010
Hey! What's the matter, Nirvash?

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:36.440
I don't wanna hear any of your mukyuus!
Don't move on your own, damn it!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.330
Stop! Stop, I said!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.480
Nirvash has bailed out!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.520
Bailed out?!

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.270
Keep it together!
He fell off his board, that's all!

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:51.160
He wasn't shot down!

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.950
Ow...

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:08.080
Nirvash? Is that you? Is it really you?

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:16.090
Eureka? Eureka, is that you?

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.990
No way! Renton?

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.220
Renton, is it you?

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.120
Is that really you, Renton?!

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:26.270
Nirvash contact with target confirmed!

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:29.830
Coordinates: 0080 by 0083!

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.700
Send retrieval orders to the mobile units!

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:32.480
Roger!

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:36.010
I can't believe our rookie managed to
break through that cordon by himself...

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:38.560
Is it a simple coincidence?

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:42.200
Or is there some strange power at work here?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:42.630
"Myth Regeneration Project"

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:44.830
As people who have roles
to play in the myth...
"Myth Regeneration Project"

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.830
"Myth Regeneration Project"

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.650
I always believed it. All this time,
I believed that I'd see you one day.
"Myth Regeneration Project"

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:50.660
I always believed it. All this time,
I believed that I'd see you one day.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:54.940
I missed you! I missed you so much!

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:56.190
I...

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:59.010
Eureka!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:03.470
It's a miracle... Right at the very end,
a miracle happened.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:07.390
Renton, it really <i>is </i>you!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.720
I missed you so much, too...

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:15.360
Uh-oh...

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:20.640
Let's go, Eureka! Quick, get in!

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.870
I'm sorry, I can't go.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:25.600
What're you talking about?

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.790
If we don't hurry,
the EIZO are gonna be all over us!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:28.830
That's just it!
If we don't hurry,
the EIZO are gonna be all over us!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.080
If you stay here, you'll get
caught in the attack!

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:34.760
If you stay with me,
you'll die along with me, Renton!

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:37.370
I won't let that happen, no matter what!

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.760
No matter what!

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:49.340
EIZO halt confirmed!

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:50.480
Because of that light just now?

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.480
Unknown!

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:53.000
Message from the flagship Shinano!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:58.790
As of now, South Dakota is abandoned!
All forces, fall back to line 5-5-7!

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:01.240
Could the secret item have halted the EIZO?

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:03.500
Stellar wave detected!

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:05.410
This is bad! It's a fusion phenomenon!

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.960
What are the estimated coordinates?

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:09.960
Coordinates: 0080 by 0083!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:10.580
It can't be!

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:27.230
S-Signals of the objective
and Nirvash, both lost...

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.160
It was over before it began...

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:31.900
Holland?!

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:36.480
Our dreams... Hell, our whole future...
just went up in smoke.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.540
Dammit!

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:44.370
Eureka! Eureka!

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.910
Talk to me, Eureka! Eureka!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:51.480
I warned you... After I tried
so hard to warn you...

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.580
Why did you get involved, Renton?!

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:58.620
What're you saying?
Who else is gonna protect you?!

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:00.630
I don't <i>want </i>you to protect me!

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:05.910
I'm not worth saving! I don't
deserve you protecting me, Renton!

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:07.400
That's not your decision to make!

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:09.700
Don't decide that on your own...

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.480
Don't decide something like that on your own!

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:17.290
After you were taken away, I swore to myself.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:19.300
That I'd never let that happen again!

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:24.790
That if I ever saw you again,
I'd keep you safe, no matter what!

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.740
So please... come with me, Eureka!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:35.410
Renton, I... The truth is...

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:37.750
...I don't want to leave you, either.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.420
I want to stay with--

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.540
Eureka... Eureka...

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:55.040
Eureka... Eureka... Eureka!

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:57.250
Eureka! Eureka!

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:58.750
Eureka!

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:08.160
Renton... Renton... Renton...

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.120
Renton! Renton! Renton!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:13.540
Renton! Renton!

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:23.620
Oh... This is the world
that Renton always saw.

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:25.820
The world that I've always wanted to see.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:27.260
But...

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:30.550
it hurts. It hurts...

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:34.620
Save me... Save me, Renton!

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:40.610
Nirvash!

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.400
Eureka!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.410
Renton! Renton!

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:50.950
I've got you!

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:56.270
I won't let you go! I won't let you go--
never again, Eureka!

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.750
Idiot! Idiot, idiot, idiot!

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.380
You're such an idiot, Renton!

00:22:03.200 --> 00:22:06.500
You're an idiot. You're
such a big idiot, Renton.

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:09.410
You did something so reckless
to help the likes of me...

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:10.640
I can't stand it.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:14.270
I can't stand being apart from you anymore!

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:16.270
Renton...

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:20.320
Neither can I. I feel the same.

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:29.740
The Gekko is now crossing line 5-5-7.

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:32.700
Now exiting the EIZO's
interference wave zone.

00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:35.870
What the hell? A new interference
wave source has appeared!

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:36.710
Reinforcements?

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:38.300
No! It's something else!

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:40.250
What's the location? Where's it coming from?!

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:44.840
Code 0080 by 0083!
Right below the South Dakota tower!

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:45.920
What did you say?

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:47.620
Stellar wave detected!

00:22:47.620 --> 00:22:51.120
I-It's no use! The gain is so high
it's impossible to measure!

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:52.200
It's the same.

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:53.620
What is?

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:57.540
It's the same as that other time.
It's the same as the rainbow from before!

00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:09.870
What happened?

00:23:09.870 --> 00:23:11.180
I have no idea.

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:17.120
But it's as if the world is singing
a song of joy about something...

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.580
Amazing! That was amazing, Nirvash!

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:38.850
What is this? What's happening?

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.060
Renton! Ahead!

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:43.690
What do you mean, it's okay?

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:06.760
The EIZO... They turned into clouds...

00:24:07.120 --> 00:24:07.840
Eureka?!

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:10.060
I'm okay...

00:24:10.450 --> 00:24:11.300
Eureka!

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:34.200
You're absolutely sure?

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:35.630
Yes, sir! It's the Nirvash!

00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:38.200
I'm also picking up an
additional two life signs!

00:24:38.200 --> 00:24:41.950
So that flash of light was stardust?

00:24:41.950 --> 00:24:44.750
There's nothing in the data
to support that conclusion.

00:24:44.750 --> 00:24:45.530
I see.

00:24:46.330 --> 00:24:47.220
Still...

00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:51.300
...we ended up getting our hands
on the key to our objective, right?

00:24:51.410 --> 00:24:57.640
Right. That's the linchpin to our real objective,
the Myth Regeneration Project.

00:24:57.870 --> 00:25:00.220
That has to be the "White Sacred One"...

00:25:06.250 --> 00:25:08.250
Eureka, hang in there!

00:25:08.250 --> 00:25:09.530
I'll be all right...

00:25:09.910 --> 00:25:13.530
Compared to the experiments the
military put me through, this is nothing...

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.280
It'll be over soon? What will be over soon?

00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:21.160
S-Send them away?

00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:22.360
What is it?

00:25:22.360 --> 00:25:23.960
Nirvash says he's gonna...

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:28.540
...send the EIZO away for us!

00:26:11.580 --> 00:26:12.950
You okay, Renton?

00:26:15.540 --> 00:26:16.660
Commander...

00:26:16.660 --> 00:26:18.970
That was a little too much
grandstanding on your part.

00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:21.830
But for your first mission, you fought hard.

00:26:21.830 --> 00:26:24.810
And you even successfully
retrieved the top-secret item.

00:26:25.290 --> 00:26:26.480
You did good, kid.

00:26:27.010 --> 00:26:30.120
Top-secret item?

00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:35.820
That's right. That girl is Eureka,
the military's top secret.

00:26:37.580 --> 00:26:41.660
Commander. What do you mean by that?

00:26:44.250 --> 00:26:47.500
Those are the basic facts of the case.

00:26:47.500 --> 00:26:49.950
The one item that I find troubling

00:26:49.950 --> 00:26:55.330
is the syringe containing the drug
"datu-RA" that was left at the scene.

00:26:55.330 --> 00:26:57.050
datu-RA? I'm unfamiliar with the name.

00:26:57.050 --> 00:27:00.910
It is a drug that is administered to
survivors of the Tragedy of Doha.

00:27:00.910 --> 00:27:05.120
Of course, considering that the victim
was Major General Dewey Sörenstam...

00:27:05.120 --> 00:27:08.120
...a man who earned his fame
at the Tragedy of Doha,

00:27:08.120 --> 00:27:12.800
the fact that it was found at the
crime scene is hardly surprising.

00:27:13.540 --> 00:27:14.970
This concludes my report.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:17.010
If you will excuse me.

00:27:17.830 --> 00:27:20.220
A moment, please, Comrade Coda.

00:27:20.950 --> 00:27:21.820
Yes, what is it?

00:27:22.290 --> 00:27:26.080
Forgive me, but might I trouble you
to stay with us for one more week?

00:27:27.620 --> 00:27:32.580
The week prior to retirement is
to be spent however one sees fit.

00:27:32.830 --> 00:27:35.640
Surely I don't have to remind you
that this is guaranteed by law.

00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:39.970
We are about to enter the final stage
of the Hammer of God project,

00:27:40.290 --> 00:27:45.040
so we can't spare any personnel on
this Dewey Sörenstam murder, you see.

00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:47.950
As luck would have it, we happen
to have a politician right here

00:27:47.950 --> 00:27:50.750
with a background in public security
who has nothing better to do.

00:27:50.750 --> 00:27:51.980
Is this an order?

00:27:52.380 --> 00:27:57.580
You were hoping for a berth
on the escape ship, as I recall...

00:28:00.750 --> 00:28:02.870
Looks like we've given them the slip.

00:28:02.870 --> 00:28:08.540
Yeah. We'll probably be spotted soon,
but no one can catch up to us now.

00:28:08.540 --> 00:28:11.450
All that's left now is to get
our hands on the stardust.

00:28:11.450 --> 00:28:15.510
When we do, our dreams...
your dream and mine... will come true.

00:28:16.120 --> 00:28:18.870
You won't have to suffer anymore.

00:28:19.700 --> 00:28:21.120
It won't be long, will it?

00:28:22.120 --> 00:28:23.550
Not long at all.

00:28:24.410 --> 00:28:26.970
Our future is almost close enough to touch.

00:28:27.700 --> 00:28:31.030
"Clad in stardust, the White Sacred One...

00:28:31.620 --> 00:28:35.480
...will erect a rainbow bridge to
the stars with the waning moon,

00:28:35.910 --> 00:28:40.190
and the chosen maiden and boy
will return to the blue orb...

00:28:40.950 --> 00:28:43.530
...all that which was born from the earth."

00:28:50.410 --> 00:28:51.510
Renton...

00:28:52.160 --> 00:28:57.120
Um... The doctor said
I could have five minutes.

00:28:57.750 --> 00:28:59.940
So, um... I...

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:03.750
You've grown, Renton.

00:29:06.290 --> 00:29:09.140
You, too, Eureka. You're really pretty now.

00:29:12.580 --> 00:29:13.800
It's the same.

00:29:13.800 --> 00:29:14.790
What is?

00:29:15.230 --> 00:29:16.760
This--it's just like when we first met.

00:29:17.290 --> 00:29:19.790
Really? If you say so...

00:29:19.790 --> 00:29:26.990
Just like now, I was lying in bed,
and when I woke up, there you were.

00:29:27.370 --> 00:29:28.530
It was Nirvash.

00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:32.800
That day, Nirvash had disappeared.

00:29:33.700 --> 00:29:36.790
I'd looked for him all over the hospital,

00:29:36.790 --> 00:29:40.090
and then I heard his voice
coming from your room.

00:29:40.500 --> 00:29:42.370
And when I went inside, there you were.

00:29:42.950 --> 00:29:48.970
Renton, do you remember?
You said something when you saw me.

00:29:50.950 --> 00:29:53.040
Sorry, I don't remember.

00:29:53.540 --> 00:29:54.540
You said I was pretty.

00:29:55.330 --> 00:29:59.010
When you looked at me, you said I was pretty.

00:30:03.370 --> 00:30:04.910
What a lousy piece of luck!

00:30:04.910 --> 00:30:06.830
This is no laughing matter.

00:30:06.830 --> 00:30:11.000
So, the Public Security Director
has picked me up in his personal car.

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:14.580
I can assume that there have
been developments, Jurgens?

00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:17.000
The late Maj. Gen. Dewey Sörenstam.

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:20.580
Arrest warrants have been issued for
the soldiers who served under him.

00:30:20.580 --> 00:30:24.120
Arrest warrants? On suspicion
of assassinating the general?

00:30:24.120 --> 00:30:27.130
No. On suspicion of abducting minors.

00:30:27.410 --> 00:30:28.750
What do you mean?

00:30:29.270 --> 00:30:33.290
Had you heard that Maj. Gen. Sörenstam
took in war orphans on his own initiative?

00:30:33.290 --> 00:30:34.430
Only rumors.

00:30:34.910 --> 00:30:40.500
Apparently, those orphans have been
missing since just after the murder.

00:30:40.500 --> 00:30:45.280
Were you aware that Maj. Gen. Sörenstam
had some... unusual interests?

00:30:45.570 --> 00:30:47.780
Unusual interests?

00:30:48.040 --> 00:30:51.200
It would seem that he had no
interest in the bodies of adults.

00:30:52.120 --> 00:30:56.830
Given the current state of affairs,
it would have been simple to collect children.

00:30:56.830 --> 00:31:00.000
He did this to war orphans?
That's disgusting.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.080
It's possible that this was
the reason he was the first

00:31:03.080 --> 00:31:05.650
to rush to the scene at the
time of the Tragedy of Doha.

00:31:06.140 --> 00:31:09.370
I swear, you should never
look too closely at heroes...

00:31:10.540 --> 00:31:13.860
So, his fellow soldiers couldn't turn a blind
eye to his behavior and assassinated him,

00:31:13.860 --> 00:31:15.290
and then absconded with the children.

00:31:15.290 --> 00:31:18.410
That would certainly fit the evidence.

00:31:18.410 --> 00:31:20.150
This would be a major scandal.

00:31:20.690 --> 00:31:22.560
I don't blame the army for
wanting to keep this quiet.

00:31:23.190 --> 00:31:25.430
So, do you have any likely suspects?

00:31:26.260 --> 00:31:28.920
We're using all our resources
to track down this man,

00:31:28.920 --> 00:31:32.160
a former subordinate of the general's,
and his associates.

00:31:32.750 --> 00:31:34.580
His name is Holland Novak.

00:31:34.950 --> 00:31:36.400
Holland Novak...

00:31:37.370 --> 00:31:38.160
Excuse me.

00:31:38.370 --> 00:31:40.290
--This man? Really?
--It's me. What?!

00:31:41.160 --> 00:31:43.630
He hardly strikes me as the type
who is driven by a sense of justice.

00:31:44.120 --> 00:31:47.000
Understood. I'll make
arrangements immediately.

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:48.160
What is it?

00:31:48.160 --> 00:31:49.970
A class-1 investigation order.

00:31:50.660 --> 00:31:55.760
We've learned that the unit that recovered
the top-secret item, the 303rd D.R.,

00:31:55.760 --> 00:31:58.160
went missing with the item
right after the operation.

00:31:58.160 --> 00:31:59.310
Went missing?!

00:32:00.480 --> 00:32:03.310
When this operation is over,
I can make 2nd lieutenant.

00:32:04.060 --> 00:32:07.540
And when you make 2nd lieutenant,
you can choose where you get stationed.

00:32:07.540 --> 00:32:11.890
I think I'll ask to be stationed
at the Warsaw garrison.

00:32:12.500 --> 00:32:17.410
If I get approval,
let's go back together, Eureka.

00:32:18.040 --> 00:32:22.080
Let's live together in Warsaw
and watch over that hill.

00:32:22.420 --> 00:32:23.300
Together.

00:32:23.610 --> 00:32:24.270
Idiot.

00:32:24.950 --> 00:32:28.230
Idiot? What makes me an idiot?

00:32:28.790 --> 00:32:31.010
We promised the Professor, remember?!

00:32:31.570 --> 00:32:34.190
I want to keep our promise, too.

00:32:34.700 --> 00:32:37.010
But that's impossible now.

00:32:37.270 --> 00:32:39.000
For one thing, I'm not human.

00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:42.660
So what if you're not?!
We were never any different!

00:32:42.660 --> 00:32:46.200
My mom, my dad, even the Professor...

00:32:46.200 --> 00:32:49.620
They all cared for you just
as much as they did for me!

00:32:50.030 --> 00:32:51.200
It's always been like that.

00:32:51.200 --> 00:32:53.660
You're the only one who's ever
said things like that to me.

00:32:54.660 --> 00:32:59.910
Tell me... Do you know why they
call me the military's top secret?

00:32:59.910 --> 00:33:01.480
I don't know.

00:33:01.480 --> 00:33:04.330
The Commander won't tell me,
and neither will anybody else.

00:33:04.680 --> 00:33:09.440
It's because I'm a spy robot
that the EIZO sent here.

00:33:10.440 --> 00:33:15.050
A robot made by the EIZO to
gather information on humanity.

00:33:15.470 --> 00:33:16.570
That's what I am.

00:33:18.250 --> 00:33:19.790
Quit kidding around...

00:33:19.790 --> 00:33:21.440
You don't believe me?

00:33:22.830 --> 00:33:28.020
But that's all right. I want to be
an ordinary girl around you, Renton.

00:33:29.080 --> 00:33:30.790
So anyway, here's my story...

00:33:30.790 --> 00:33:34.790
After that, Eureka started
telling me about herself

00:33:34.790 --> 00:33:36.830
as if she was delirious from a fever.

00:33:37.460 --> 00:33:40.790
About how she was subjected to horrible
experiments after the military took her.

00:33:40.790 --> 00:33:42.500
About how she tried to die countless times.

00:33:43.290 --> 00:33:46.970
But each time, she'd look at
her pendant, and that stopped her.

00:33:47.750 --> 00:33:55.840
But the military scientists told her that
her body's functions would cease soon.

00:33:55.840 --> 00:33:57.570
In other words, that she would die.

00:33:58.080 --> 00:34:04.040
That when the red lines in
her lavender eyes disappeared,

00:34:04.040 --> 00:34:06.350
that's when she would die.

00:34:07.700 --> 00:34:10.950
Eureka said she didn't mind
if I didn't believe her.

00:34:11.540 --> 00:34:13.520
But I...

00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:15.940
There's no time to lose.

00:34:17.520 --> 00:34:21.160
If I'm going to take Eureka back with me
to Warsaw, there's not much time.

00:34:21.750 --> 00:34:24.870
So you'll help me out, right, Nirvash?

00:34:28.160 --> 00:34:29.840
Why aren't you saying anything?

00:34:31.640 --> 00:34:33.240
You sure are fickle...

00:34:37.080 --> 00:34:39.640
Please don't take it so hard, ma'am.

00:34:40.040 --> 00:34:43.290
The fact that the culprit behind
Maj. Gen. Sörenstam's killing

00:34:43.290 --> 00:34:49.330
was the leader of the missing
303rd Regiment was no fault of ours.

00:34:49.650 --> 00:34:51.200
There's one thing that still bothers me.

00:34:51.200 --> 00:34:52.410
Ma'am?

00:34:53.160 --> 00:34:58.030
Why do you suppose a syringe containing
datu-RA was left at the murder scene?

00:34:58.660 --> 00:35:02.920
The only people there were the general and
Holland Novak, a low-ranking soldier, right?

00:35:03.450 --> 00:35:06.040
You believe that someone else
was in the room, ma'am?

00:35:06.830 --> 00:35:14.220
Do you know what sort of effect the drug
MM-88, commonly known as datu-RA, has?

00:35:14.620 --> 00:35:16.190
No, ma'am, I don't.

00:35:16.680 --> 00:35:18.210
The drug acts as a growth inhibitor.

00:35:19.310 --> 00:35:24.260
The drug is a growth inhibitor.
In simple terms, it's an immortality elixir.

00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.870
Of course, its effects
only last for seven days.

00:35:27.870 --> 00:35:30.790
Ordinary citizens would probably
see the drug as somewhat pointless.

00:35:30.790 --> 00:35:34.860
Wait, ma'am. Why would the
General have such a useless drug?

00:35:34.860 --> 00:35:38.520
It's not as if that man had
any particular need for it.

00:35:39.040 --> 00:35:40.620
The one who needed it was--

00:35:40.620 --> 00:35:42.410
Please pardon the intrusion
in your off time, ma'am.

00:35:42.950 --> 00:35:46.580
This is Minister Coda's private residence!
How dare you barge in?!

00:35:46.580 --> 00:35:50.500
This is an emergency.
Holland Novak has been located.

00:35:50.500 --> 00:35:52.910
I see. That was simpler than I expected.

00:35:52.910 --> 00:35:54.130
You misunderstand me!

00:35:54.390 --> 00:35:57.590
What they found is Holland Novak's corpse!

00:35:59.080 --> 00:36:04.830
Wait. If he's dead, then who is
the leader of the 303rd Regiment?

00:36:06.040 --> 00:36:10.390
Attention Gekko, this is
the Liberation Army...

00:36:10.390 --> 00:36:12.500
...Eastern Front 277th Mobile Division.

00:36:12.500 --> 00:36:15.870
Heave to and submit to a spot
inspection immediately. I say again...

00:36:15.870 --> 00:36:17.460
Has everyone had their injection?

00:36:17.460 --> 00:36:19.980
You're the last, 350Z.

00:36:20.950 --> 00:36:23.490
Everyone on board has finished
taking their shot, too.

00:36:23.900 --> 00:36:27.580
350Z... That really takes me back.

00:36:27.580 --> 00:36:30.100
But that isn't my real name.

00:36:31.080 --> 00:36:33.720
We had our names and our
future stolen from us.

00:36:34.830 --> 00:36:37.590
But we'll be able to take
them both back soon.

00:36:37.950 --> 00:36:40.000
Through our own actions.

00:36:41.330 --> 00:36:42.430
I know.

00:36:42.870 --> 00:36:47.370
All hands, prepare for torpedo attack!
Switch IKF to Phase Ageha!

00:36:47.370 --> 00:36:48.430
Aye aye!

00:36:56.620 --> 00:36:57.360
An attack?!

00:36:58.750 --> 00:37:02.870
What's going on?
There was no scramble order...

00:37:02.870 --> 00:37:05.990
And this IKF phase, it's...

00:37:05.990 --> 00:37:07.910
What the heck is going on?!

00:37:12.290 --> 00:37:14.880
That's an advanced Liberation
Army battleship!

00:37:25.040 --> 00:37:28.470
What's going on?
Why are we fighting our allies?!

00:37:29.500 --> 00:37:31.730
Commander?! Do you read me, Commander?

00:37:31.870 --> 00:37:34.910
What's wrong? What happened?

00:37:36.910 --> 00:37:38.910
Nobody told you to come out here!

00:37:38.910 --> 00:37:41.240
Nobody gave you orders to go into battle!

00:37:41.370 --> 00:37:45.210
Matthieu! Why's the Commander
fighting the army?

00:37:45.210 --> 00:37:47.470
Are those guys a rebel squadron or something?

00:37:47.470 --> 00:37:49.280
No, they ain't!

00:37:49.290 --> 00:37:52.710
The only rebel outfit around here is us.

00:37:58.790 --> 00:37:59.750
Nirvash!

00:37:59.870 --> 00:38:01.620
Hey, Nirvash!

00:38:03.090 --> 00:38:04.260
He used your kill switch?

00:38:05.650 --> 00:38:10.260
Commander?! What's going on?!
Why are you doing this?! Please, stop!

00:38:10.330 --> 00:38:12.500
They're humans, just like us!

00:38:12.500 --> 00:38:16.560
That'd be true, if we were normal humans.

00:38:17.450 --> 00:38:23.990
If we were normal humans,
we wouldn't be doing this!

00:38:24.410 --> 00:38:26.860
Wait, Commander! Commander!

00:38:26.860 --> 00:38:29.450
Commander! Commander! Commander!

00:38:29.450 --> 00:38:29.530
Commander!!
Commander! Commander! Commander!

00:38:29.530 --> 00:38:31.030
Commander!!

00:38:36.200 --> 00:38:39.330
Their plan thus far was sheer genius.

00:38:39.330 --> 00:38:41.910
The leader assassinated
Maj. Gen. Dewey Sörenstam,

00:38:41.910 --> 00:38:44.870
then murdered their guardian, Holland Novak.

00:38:44.870 --> 00:38:48.750
Then he posed as Novak and
infiltrated the army as a mercenary,

00:38:48.750 --> 00:38:51.250
and then, after stealing the top-secret item,

00:38:51.250 --> 00:38:56.230
he used the confusion of that unknown
EIZO phenomenon to cover his tracks.

00:38:58.620 --> 00:39:01.440
I have no idea what their objective is,

00:39:01.870 --> 00:39:05.380
but we know at the very least that
this whole incident is the work

00:39:05.380 --> 00:39:08.500
of the boys and girls who
survived the Tragedy of Doha.

00:39:09.500 --> 00:39:11.530
But that leaves just one odd point.

00:39:12.660 --> 00:39:17.580
Not all of the 303rd Regiment are
survivors of the Tragedy of Doha.

00:39:17.910 --> 00:39:19.120
Some aren't?

00:39:19.450 --> 00:39:21.300
Yes, ma'am. Just one.

00:39:22.130 --> 00:39:27.000
This one young soldier, Renton Thurston,
doesn't match our database.

00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:29.550
Renton... Thurston?!

00:39:30.290 --> 00:39:34.430
Corporal Renton Thurston.
Age: 14. Place of birth: Warsaw.

00:39:34.660 --> 00:39:37.430
Parents were the masterminds
behind the Tragedy of Doha.

00:39:37.800 --> 00:39:39.540
Both parents are deceased.

00:39:39.540 --> 00:39:44.570
After his father died in combat, he enrolled
in Suginami, Tokyo's PLA Children's School.

00:39:44.780 --> 00:39:48.290
Although he was subjected to
severe abuse as the child of cultists,

00:39:48.290 --> 00:39:50.950
he exhibited superior skills as a mech pilot.

00:39:59.790 --> 00:40:04.000
It is believed that this skill is the result
of his ability to achieve a rapport

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:08.910
with a KLF larva that he
grew up with named Nirvash.

00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:16.660
In fact, Nirvash's unparalleled rapid
growth is proof of those abilities.

00:40:16.660 --> 00:40:19.910
After it was confirmed that
he'd destroyed three top dogs

00:40:19.910 --> 00:40:23.980
in a mock combat drill after
being re-outfitted as a KLF,

00:40:23.980 --> 00:40:28.000
a request came down in December 2054
from the PLA 1st Mobile Division

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:31.750
asking that he be allowed in as a
special exception, and he accepted.

00:40:31.750 --> 00:40:34.330
You'll give me a special promotion
to 2nd lieutenant, right?

00:40:34.750 --> 00:40:40.040
That same month, he was assigned to
the 1st Mobile Division, 303rd D.R.,

00:40:40.250 --> 00:40:43.910
and ever since the engagement with
the EIZO in South Dakota last month,

00:40:43.910 --> 00:40:47.120
he has been in hiding along with his team.

00:40:49.250 --> 00:40:53.070
He's gone through so much,
and he's only 14... It's cruel.

00:40:53.660 --> 00:40:56.500
A boy who has a grudge against society, hm?

00:40:57.330 --> 00:40:59.680
You believe he is a member
of the rebels, then?

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:05.450
Not only that, but a key figure.
Perhaps it's a valid line of thought.

00:41:05.450 --> 00:41:07.170
Thank you for waiting, Excellency.

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:11.110
If you will follow me,
please. Right this way.

00:41:12.660 --> 00:41:14.040
Is everything ready?

00:41:14.040 --> 00:41:16.830
All participating members are synched.

00:41:16.830 --> 00:41:18.370
Do we record this?

00:41:18.370 --> 00:41:21.120
Nah, I don't see any need to.
All right, let's start.

00:41:22.540 --> 00:41:24.340
Lift your head, Renton.

00:41:25.080 --> 00:41:27.160
Don't want to look a
traitor in the face, huh?

00:41:28.720 --> 00:41:30.580
So, you were all in on this.

00:41:30.580 --> 00:41:33.620
That's right. Sorry we had to deceive you.

00:41:33.620 --> 00:41:35.160
What are you after?

00:41:35.160 --> 00:41:40.080
What's your reason for tricking me,
stealing Eureka, and turning rebel?

00:41:40.080 --> 00:41:44.400
Before I answer that, there's one
thing that I want to ask you.

00:41:44.400 --> 00:41:46.900
How old do I look to you?

00:41:47.120 --> 00:41:48.080
Come again?

00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:49.400
Come on, answer the question.

00:41:49.960 --> 00:41:51.410
How the hell should I know?

00:41:51.410 --> 00:41:52.720
I'm 17.

00:41:53.700 --> 00:42:00.790
And not just me. Everyone here,
every member of the 303rd, is 17.

00:42:02.080 --> 00:42:05.450
Have you heard of the Children of Neverland?

00:42:05.450 --> 00:42:08.080
You don't mean Peter Pan, I take it?

00:42:08.080 --> 00:42:10.590
The Tragedy of Doha,
which happened eight years ago.

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:15.020
The boys and girls of unknown origin who
were found at the heart of the explosion...

00:42:15.620 --> 00:42:17.590
That's the name they gave themselves.

00:42:17.950 --> 00:42:23.270
I was given to understand that this place
is why those "eternal children" appeared.

00:42:25.200 --> 00:42:27.330
The people here at the old Warsaw Labs

00:42:27.330 --> 00:42:30.750
were conducting research
into anti-EIZO weaponry.

00:42:30.750 --> 00:42:34.750
This is also the birthplace
of the KLFs that we use.

00:42:34.750 --> 00:42:40.170
So you are saying that "wisdom" beyond
human understanding was collected here?

00:42:40.170 --> 00:42:43.420
Yes, ma'am. And the source
of all that "wisdom"

00:42:43.420 --> 00:42:46.750
was the humanoid EIZO that were
found every so often on the battlefield.

00:42:46.750 --> 00:42:50.750
These are the girls that we refer
to as our top-secret items.

00:42:51.700 --> 00:42:53.710
The girls... plural?

00:42:53.710 --> 00:42:57.330
Yes, ma'am. There have been
seven that we know of.

00:42:57.330 --> 00:43:02.790
The girls were tortured to try to glean
information about the EIZO from them.

00:43:02.790 --> 00:43:07.540
And in the course of time, the people
here gradually developed into a cult.

00:43:07.540 --> 00:43:09.270
What did they uncover?

00:43:09.620 --> 00:43:16.160
I don't know. All records were burned
because the local residents were enraged.

00:43:16.160 --> 00:43:17.180
I see.

00:43:17.730 --> 00:43:20.700
However, based on the few that remain,

00:43:20.700 --> 00:43:24.290
we know that they conducted
experiments on forty war orphans

00:43:24.290 --> 00:43:29.290
and one of the girls that were meant
to carry out a project of some sort.

00:43:30.580 --> 00:43:35.960
They used subject No. 006,
a girl code-named Anemone.

00:43:37.450 --> 00:43:40.680
By the time we figured
it out, it was too late.

00:43:41.160 --> 00:43:44.940
The ship we were on was on
a direct course for the EIZO.

00:43:45.770 --> 00:43:50.550
The only adults on board were a young
soldier and a pink-haired woman.

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:55.850
They just stood there holding each other,
as if they knew something was coming.

00:43:57.820 --> 00:44:00.410
Before long, everything around us started
glowing with a rainbow-colored light.

00:44:00.820 --> 00:44:05.450
The next thing we knew, we were being
thrown out of the disintegrating ship.

00:44:07.120 --> 00:44:08.830
I thought I was going to die.

00:44:09.400 --> 00:44:13.420
Inside the rainbow tunnel,
our bodies started to disintegrate.

00:44:15.120 --> 00:44:18.350
And then it hit me.
We'd been used as guinea pigs.

00:44:19.910 --> 00:44:24.430
No one would shed a tear
over the loss of us orphans.

00:44:24.580 --> 00:44:26.930
I bet that's what the adults thought.

00:44:27.290 --> 00:44:31.310
But then we saw something when we
came out the other end of that tunnel.

00:44:31.520 --> 00:44:32.070
"Renton" "Eureka"

00:44:32.070 --> 00:44:33.810
A world spread out before us.
"Renton" "Eureka"

00:44:33.810 --> 00:44:34.450
"Renton" "Eureka"

00:44:34.450 --> 00:44:37.960
A blue world encircled with a ring of green,
with an engraved moon floating over it.
"Renton" "Eureka"

00:44:37.960 --> 00:44:40.120
A blue world encircled with a ring of green,
with an engraved moon floating over it.

00:44:42.870 --> 00:44:44.660
That's when we knew.

00:44:44.660 --> 00:44:48.680
<i>That </i>was the world that we truly belonged in.

00:44:49.870 --> 00:44:54.130
So in that regard, we owe a debt
of gratitude to your parents.

00:44:55.250 --> 00:44:56.460
What's that supposed to mean?

00:44:56.620 --> 00:44:59.200
The experiment that we
were forced to participate in

00:44:59.200 --> 00:45:02.490
came to be called the Tragedy of Doha.

00:45:03.750 --> 00:45:06.330
According to the analysis of
the People's Science Institute,

00:45:06.330 --> 00:45:09.850
the supergraviton collapse that
occurred during the Tragedy of Doha

00:45:09.850 --> 00:45:14.120
triggered the formation of a black hole
on Earth that lasted for several seconds.

00:45:14.790 --> 00:45:17.650
But, well, there's an
interesting story there.

00:45:18.370 --> 00:45:22.120
There's a theory that this
scientific breakthrough

00:45:22.120 --> 00:45:25.770
was the result of the Warsaw cult
group deciphering a certain story.

00:45:26.200 --> 00:45:27.370
A story?

00:45:27.370 --> 00:45:28.040
Yes, ma'am.

00:45:28.410 --> 00:45:31.040
And this is what they called the story.

00:45:31.040 --> 00:45:31.600
"The Ageha Myth"

00:45:31.600 --> 00:45:33.210
The Ageha Myth.
"The Ageha Myth"

00:45:33.210 --> 00:45:33.870
"The Ageha Myth"

00:45:33.870 --> 00:45:34.920
When we came to, we'd been
pulled back into this world.
"The Ageha Myth"

00:45:34.920 --> 00:45:38.270
When we came to, we'd been
pulled back into this world.

00:45:39.040 --> 00:45:42.810
The pink-haired woman and the
soldier were nowhere to be found.

00:45:43.660 --> 00:45:46.160
The military personnel who retrieved us

00:45:46.160 --> 00:45:51.790
found that we were aging at
three times the normal rate.

00:45:53.040 --> 00:45:57.300
As long as we stay here in this world,
all that's waiting for us is death.

00:45:58.450 --> 00:45:59.820
But I say screw that.

00:46:00.500 --> 00:46:03.940
We've been screwed over by fate,
our bodies have been shattered,

00:46:04.530 --> 00:46:06.950
and even our futures have
been stolen from us.

00:46:06.950 --> 00:46:08.910
I say screw that!

00:46:08.910 --> 00:46:12.600
No way am I going to accept a life like that!

00:46:13.140 --> 00:46:14.540
Cry me a river.

00:46:14.540 --> 00:46:15.250
What?

00:46:16.620 --> 00:46:20.460
Even so, that doesn't give you the
right to go around killing people!

00:46:21.350 --> 00:46:26.010
You people are scum. You're a
bunch of murdering bastards!

00:46:29.700 --> 00:46:30.850
Get this straight, kid.

00:46:31.200 --> 00:46:33.310
No matter what you do from now on,

00:46:33.310 --> 00:46:37.370
as far as the world's concerned, you'll always
be a willing member of a rebel crew!

00:46:42.250 --> 00:46:45.620
You know that all matter
that exists in this world,

00:46:45.620 --> 00:46:48.770
us humans included,
is comprised of atoms, yes?

00:46:49.240 --> 00:46:53.420
Those atoms in turn are
composed of tiny particles.

00:46:53.870 --> 00:46:58.790
The smallest particles we've proven
so far are called elementary particles.

00:46:58.790 --> 00:47:04.410
However, instead of being in a fixed state,
these particles ebb and flow.

00:47:04.410 --> 00:47:06.870
Ebb and flow? You mean like waves?

00:47:06.870 --> 00:47:10.890
Yes. This means that if one
could control these waves,

00:47:10.890 --> 00:47:15.540
it would even be theoretically possible
to remake the world as one saw fit.

00:47:15.540 --> 00:47:19.770
It was the Tragedy of Doha eight years
ago that substantiated this theory.

00:47:20.250 --> 00:47:25.450
The pions detected during the event
should have exhibited random movement...

00:47:25.450 --> 00:47:28.450
...but their movement actually bore a
striking resemblance to a certain pattern.

00:47:28.450 --> 00:47:31.410
When they sleep, humans dream, right?

00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:36.870
Their movement was identical to
EEG readings taken during REM sleep.

00:47:37.040 --> 00:47:41.310
You'll have to forgive me. I don't
understand where this is going.

00:47:42.370 --> 00:47:47.700
Simply put, the EIZO had a system able
to freely manipulate elementary particles,

00:47:47.700 --> 00:47:51.610
which they then tuned to someone's dreams,
and tried to remake the world.

00:47:52.200 --> 00:47:54.000
Come now, surely that isn't even...

00:47:54.620 --> 00:47:56.780
Have you ever thought about it like this?

00:47:57.910 --> 00:48:02.780
They possessed the system.
But they lacked the means to activate it.

00:48:03.500 --> 00:48:06.320
And so, they tried to make
someone throw the switch.

00:48:06.950 --> 00:48:09.760
Maybe the Ageha Myth
was the instruction manual.

00:48:10.410 --> 00:48:12.070
A booby trap...

00:48:12.450 --> 00:48:16.750
Why do you suppose the manual
took the form of a story?

00:48:16.750 --> 00:48:20.880
And this switch... What
do you suppose it was?

00:48:30.330 --> 00:48:31.510
It's no surprise...

00:48:33.090 --> 00:48:35.350
After all, I'm not even human.

00:48:38.540 --> 00:48:42.370
What did I tell you? It was a waste
of time to try to win him over.

00:48:42.370 --> 00:48:47.040
Even if Renton <i>was </i>chosen by Eureka,
in the end, he's a normal human.

00:48:47.040 --> 00:48:48.640
He's not like the rest of us.

00:48:49.790 --> 00:48:51.950
Hey, are you listening to a word I'm saying?

00:48:51.950 --> 00:48:53.580
Yeah, I'm listening.

00:48:53.580 --> 00:48:56.910
Look, Holland, we're
running out of time here.

00:48:56.910 --> 00:49:01.760
There's no telling how long we have,
even if we do keep using datu-RA.

00:49:02.250 --> 00:49:04.080
I know, I know...

00:49:04.080 --> 00:49:06.910
Do you <i>really </i>get it?

00:49:07.910 --> 00:49:10.010
Anyway, you're too optimistic.

00:49:10.010 --> 00:49:12.930
You took in Renton without any real proof.

00:49:12.930 --> 00:49:15.580
Save us all a lot of trouble, and--

00:49:15.580 --> 00:49:17.010
I <i>know</i>, damn it!

00:49:18.040 --> 00:49:19.270
I know...

00:49:19.620 --> 00:49:25.120
When we killed Sörenstam and
wiped out the 277th Mobile Unit,

00:49:25.120 --> 00:49:27.520
it was all because our survival was at stake.

00:49:27.910 --> 00:49:30.320
So you don't have to tell me
what needs to be done.

00:49:32.750 --> 00:49:38.440
Tell me, how many people do you think
we're going to kill before we're through?

00:49:41.450 --> 00:49:43.020
Hey, wait!

00:49:43.750 --> 00:49:46.670
You aren't having second thoughts, are you?

00:49:46.670 --> 00:49:47.590
Say what?

00:49:47.590 --> 00:49:49.590
It's way too late to have cold feet.

00:49:49.700 --> 00:49:51.800
<i>You </i>set all this in motion, remember?

00:49:52.700 --> 00:49:56.040
So start showing some spine, damn it!

00:49:56.040 --> 00:49:58.310
Just because we haven't
done anything to Renton

00:49:58.310 --> 00:50:01.090
doesn't make up for the crimes
we've already committed!

00:50:01.580 --> 00:50:05.910
If we inject Renton with a massive dose
of the truth serum 99T to brainwash him,

00:50:05.910 --> 00:50:08.320
we'll be able to make him
do whatever we want.

00:50:08.870 --> 00:50:13.830
But if we do that, it'll destroy his mind.
Renton will be a zombie.

00:50:13.830 --> 00:50:17.830
Maybe, but he can't be persuaded!
You saw his reaction earlier!

00:50:17.830 --> 00:50:20.330
He'll never be talked into working with us!

00:50:20.330 --> 00:50:22.750
He'll try to stop us, mark my words!

00:50:22.750 --> 00:50:23.820
I just--!

00:50:24.410 --> 00:50:25.540
I just don't want...

00:50:26.560 --> 00:50:28.840
I don't want
to hurt some little kid, that's all.

00:50:30.160 --> 00:50:33.630
When you get right down to it,
<i>we're </i>really kids, too.

00:50:38.010 --> 00:50:41.330
Alert code 2! Has the army spotted us?!

00:50:41.330 --> 00:50:43.310
There's no backing out now.

00:50:44.540 --> 00:50:49.610
After this battle is over, I'll inject
Renton with the 99T truth serum.

00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:51.370
Satisfied?

00:50:51.370 --> 00:50:52.620
Aye aye.

00:50:52.620 --> 00:50:55.040
Let's get to it. Battle stations!

00:51:05.120 --> 00:51:07.910
Confirmed! Three inbound bandits!

00:51:07.910 --> 00:51:10.340
All are Yunagi-class attack carriers!

00:51:10.340 --> 00:51:13.540
Estimated time of enemy intercept: 1706!

00:51:13.540 --> 00:51:17.890
Now that we can't use Nirvash,
I'd say we're about on an even footing.

00:51:17.890 --> 00:51:21.560
I have to ask, though,
what on earth is Talho doing?

00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:24.500
We can't even make DEFCON
announcements like this!

00:51:25.580 --> 00:51:29.730
I'd heard stories... But I had
no idea it would feel this bad.

00:51:30.080 --> 00:51:34.150
What am I gonna do...?
I'm scared. I'm so scared...

00:51:34.290 --> 00:51:35.260
Please, somebody...

00:51:37.290 --> 00:51:39.450
Talho! Talho! Talho!

00:51:39.450 --> 00:51:40.800
What's wrong, Talho?!

00:51:46.160 --> 00:51:47.580
Are you okay, Renton?

00:51:48.200 --> 00:51:49.120
Eureka?

00:51:49.450 --> 00:51:51.450
A battle's about to start.

00:51:51.450 --> 00:51:55.670
If you take advantage of all the confusion,
you'll be able to get off the ship.

00:51:57.410 --> 00:51:59.390
Eureka? Your wounds, they're...

00:51:59.950 --> 00:52:03.830
The crew of the ship say that they're
going to brainwash you, Renton.

00:52:03.830 --> 00:52:06.240
I'm not about to let them do that to you.

00:52:07.330 --> 00:52:08.630
So please, hurry up and run.

00:52:09.040 --> 00:52:10.870
Hey, slow down a minute!
What are you saying--

00:52:10.870 --> 00:52:11.690
Please!

00:52:12.870 --> 00:52:13.820
Get out of here.

00:52:13.820 --> 00:52:17.410
Enemy formation currently
deployed off our starboard bow!

00:52:17.410 --> 00:52:20.410
ETA to contact is--
Enemy KLF launches detected!

00:52:20.410 --> 00:52:21.410
Count: 12!

00:52:21.410 --> 00:52:24.450
Hey, now, this fight is gonna be 4 on 1?!

00:52:24.450 --> 00:52:25.800
No, six.

00:52:26.620 --> 00:52:28.620
Hey, what's the deal with Holland?

00:52:28.620 --> 00:52:30.290
Holland is here on the bridge.

00:52:30.290 --> 00:52:32.530
He'll be commanding the ship from the bridge.

00:52:32.530 --> 00:52:35.870
Hey, wait a minute! You expect us
to fight without Holland?!

00:52:35.870 --> 00:52:38.010
--I do.
- -Get real, man!

00:52:39.040 --> 00:52:40.970
Talho isn't on the bridge...

00:52:41.910 --> 00:52:42.810
It can't be...

00:52:43.350 --> 00:52:47.080
Holland! Talho isn't in the sick bay, is she?

00:52:47.080 --> 00:52:50.230
Answer me! Talho's time hasn't
started to run out, has it?

00:52:52.250 --> 00:52:55.700
It can't be! It's too soon for that!

00:52:55.700 --> 00:52:56.700
Yeah, but...

00:52:56.700 --> 00:52:58.150
Stay cool, people!

00:52:58.750 --> 00:53:02.240
For now, focus on wiping out
the enemy that's in front of us.

00:53:02.470 --> 00:53:04.080
Holland, are you...

00:53:04.080 --> 00:53:06.940
This is no time to worry about
the life of just one person.

00:53:08.200 --> 00:53:10.330
Right now, I have to worry about the many.

00:53:10.330 --> 00:53:14.000
The lives of every person aboard this ship.

00:53:14.200 --> 00:53:15.750
Laser fire detected!

00:53:15.870 --> 00:53:17.170
AAMs inbound!

00:53:22.830 --> 00:53:26.100
Armor plating damaged!
Crap! They're proximity fuses!

00:53:26.580 --> 00:53:28.330
A show of force, huh?

00:53:28.330 --> 00:53:31.480
Okay, you sons of bitches!
We'll wipe out every last one of you!

00:53:32.620 --> 00:53:34.180
Ow...

00:53:34.540 --> 00:53:37.200
Crap, they've started.

00:53:37.200 --> 00:53:38.570
Let's get moving, Eureka!

00:53:38.910 --> 00:53:41.780
I'm sorry. But I'm staying here.

00:53:42.870 --> 00:53:46.450
What're you saying? If you
stay here, you'll die!

00:53:46.450 --> 00:53:47.530
I know that!

00:53:47.530 --> 00:53:49.090
Then why?!

00:53:49.090 --> 00:53:51.790
I <i>told</i> you. I'm not human.

00:53:51.790 --> 00:53:52.790
Eureka!

00:53:52.790 --> 00:53:54.620
I have a mission!

00:53:55.290 --> 00:53:58.710
But the thing is, I don't
want to complete it.

00:54:03.250 --> 00:54:04.720
So what's this mission?

00:54:05.410 --> 00:54:10.020
I told you. I'm a spy robot
who was sent here by the EIZO.

00:54:10.950 --> 00:54:13.370
They said the crystal that's inside me

00:54:13.370 --> 00:54:17.210
contains a record of everything
I've ever experienced on this world.

00:54:18.200 --> 00:54:23.120
They said the EIZO probably want it.
That's what the army people told me.

00:54:23.120 --> 00:54:24.540
What for?

00:54:24.540 --> 00:54:26.810
To learn humanity's weaknesses, they said.

00:54:27.440 --> 00:54:30.910
They said it was to learn
how to wipe out humanity.

00:54:32.500 --> 00:54:35.370
But I don't want that to happen.

00:54:37.620 --> 00:54:42.840
I've been through lots of terrible things.
Lots of painful and sad things, too.

00:54:43.870 --> 00:54:50.600
But if I'm going to make you suffer,
Renton, then I'd sooner die.

00:54:51.910 --> 00:54:55.640
If I die, the EIZO won't be
able to destroy humanity.

00:54:56.330 --> 00:55:00.650
If I die along with the people on this ship,
then you won't suffer anymore, Renton.

00:55:02.410 --> 00:55:06.070
I don't know what the people
on this ship are up to.

00:55:07.000 --> 00:55:11.240
All I can say for certain is that they
went after you because I was here.

00:55:11.240 --> 00:55:12.750
There's just too many of them!

00:55:12.750 --> 00:55:16.420
--If it weren't for me, you wouldn't be here.
--Can't we at least hide the Banzai Jumbo?

00:55:16.420 --> 00:55:17.950
Hide where?!

00:55:19.500 --> 00:55:20.960
We can hide in there!

00:55:21.580 --> 00:55:25.970
I'm sorry, Renton. I dragged you in--
got you involved in my own fate.

00:55:26.330 --> 00:55:29.660
All of it... It's all my fault.

00:55:31.750 --> 00:55:34.390
Even so... I was glad.

00:55:34.950 --> 00:55:37.230
I was happy that I got to
see you at the very end.

00:55:37.660 --> 00:55:39.450
It's enough for me.

00:55:41.290 --> 00:55:43.660
I don't have any regrets, not now--

00:55:43.660 --> 00:55:44.980
That's a load of crap!

00:55:45.830 --> 00:55:50.530
There you go again, deciding things
without me, making it easy just for yourself!

00:55:51.290 --> 00:55:54.750
But did you ever stop and
think about my feelings?!

00:56:03.500 --> 00:56:05.200
Damn it! It's an ambush!

00:56:05.200 --> 00:56:05.210
Sorry, guys! Hold on tight!
Damn it! It's an ambush!

00:56:05.210 --> 00:56:08.040
Sorry, guys! Hold on tight!

00:56:21.250 --> 00:56:22.310
Renton!

00:56:24.040 --> 00:56:28.370
I don't care if you're a robot
or an EIZO; it doesn't matter.

00:56:28.370 --> 00:56:31.160
I don't care what kind of fate
you're burdened with.

00:56:31.900 --> 00:56:34.940
The pounding in my heart when
we're together--that's what's real.

00:56:35.540 --> 00:56:37.790
That's what I'm feeling!

00:56:38.660 --> 00:56:42.630
Anyone who tries to take those
feelings away, I'll fight them.

00:56:42.630 --> 00:56:47.750
I don't care if it's the people on this ship,
the army, or the EIZO. I'll fight them!

00:56:47.750 --> 00:56:50.630
Renton... Please, save me.

00:56:51.160 --> 00:56:54.890
Save me from all the scary
things in the world!

00:56:55.410 --> 00:56:59.790
Multiple type-3 alarms!
Repairs during combat are impossible!

00:57:07.120 --> 00:57:09.170
Where do you think you're going, Holland?

00:57:09.540 --> 00:57:12.790
I'm going out in the Devilfish.
The bridge is yours.

00:57:12.790 --> 00:57:14.200
What the hell?

00:57:14.200 --> 00:57:14.870
Now what?!

00:57:14.870 --> 00:57:17.450
T-The catapult's opening on its own!

00:57:17.450 --> 00:57:18.200
What?!

00:57:23.040 --> 00:57:27.000
Lifesigns detected inside the Nirvash!
It's Corporal Thurston and Eureka!

00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:30.220
Those little brats... They're deserting?!

00:58:17.830 --> 00:58:21.430
Destruction of all flying
fortresses confirmed.

00:58:21.700 --> 00:58:24.330
Remaining KLFs are retreating.

00:58:25.790 --> 00:58:28.820
"Sent forth from the promised rainbow,

00:58:29.190 --> 00:58:32.190
the being shall quell the animosity
of the land without fighting."

00:58:33.040 --> 00:58:37.530
Holland, are they really
the chosen maiden and boy?

00:58:37.870 --> 00:58:39.910
Could they be Wendy and Peter?

00:58:42.200 --> 00:58:44.950
A lock-on warning? There are
still army fighters out there?

00:58:44.950 --> 00:58:49.750
The army's in retreat! The only craft
in this sector are us and our KLFs!

00:58:49.750 --> 00:58:52.290
The targeting lock is
coming from straight ahead!

00:58:52.290 --> 00:58:55.370
300 meters dead ahead!

00:59:00.080 --> 00:59:02.620
Is he going to attack the bridge directly?

00:59:03.660 --> 00:59:06.060
Are you in there, Commander Holland?

00:59:06.540 --> 00:59:07.950
I'm here, Renton.

00:59:07.950 --> 00:59:11.410
What's the matter? Why aren't you attacking?

00:59:11.410 --> 00:59:14.700
Because you haven't
answered my question yet.

00:59:14.700 --> 00:59:15.450
What?

00:59:15.950 --> 00:59:22.000
I understand who you are now.
But I don't know what you need <i>me </i>for.

00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:25.460
I don't know what you're trying
to get me and Eureka to do.

00:59:25.460 --> 00:59:28.790
What are you using us for?

00:59:30.410 --> 00:59:32.250
I thought I told you.

00:59:32.250 --> 00:59:40.720
We're trying to get back to Neverland,
that lush world, before our time runs out.

00:59:41.410 --> 00:59:44.950
To do that, we have to
recreate the Tragedy of Doha,

00:59:44.950 --> 00:59:49.620
the experiment we were forced to
participate in that was based on

00:59:49.620 --> 00:59:52.700
the Warsaw cult's Myth Regeneration Project.

00:59:52.700 --> 00:59:53.910
Recreate it?

00:59:53.910 --> 00:59:58.370
That's right. Unfortunately, the operation
we were part of was a failure,

00:59:58.370 --> 01:00:03.080
but later on, we learned that they
were already working on a new project,

01:00:03.080 --> 01:00:06.290
one using an item with a
better chance of succeeding.

01:00:06.290 --> 01:00:09.790
The Myth Regeneration Project,
Pending Issue E, No. 7.

01:00:09.790 --> 01:00:12.350
A.K.A. "Eureka Seven."

01:00:13.000 --> 01:00:15.910
When the EIZO made Eureka,
they put a crystal inside her.

01:00:15.910 --> 01:00:20.300
It contains a password meant to
allow Eureka to fuse with them.

01:00:20.870 --> 01:00:25.620
When she fuses with the EIZO,
an extradimensional door will open inside it.

01:00:25.620 --> 01:00:28.980
And the key to that door, Renton... is you.

01:00:29.830 --> 01:00:31.160
What are you talking about?

01:00:31.160 --> 01:00:34.540
I have no reason to keep talking
to someone who won't help us.

01:00:34.540 --> 01:00:36.040
What?!

01:00:36.040 --> 01:00:37.500
I have a proposal.

01:00:38.750 --> 01:00:40.860
Would you be interested
in joining forces with us?

01:00:41.660 --> 01:00:44.410
I can see how you feel about Eureka.

01:00:44.410 --> 01:00:47.250
But just like my people and I
can't survive in this world,

01:00:47.250 --> 01:00:50.870
you two can't live out your
lives together here, either.

01:00:51.950 --> 01:00:52.990
Look, Renton,

01:00:53.640 --> 01:00:55.890
we're birds of a feather.

01:00:56.590 --> 01:01:00.970
If we can just get to Neverland,
we'll be able to live out our lives.

01:01:01.620 --> 01:01:03.700
It's a fair deal, don't you think?

01:01:03.700 --> 01:01:06.140
Would someone please tell me
what the hell this "Neverland" is?

01:01:06.140 --> 01:01:08.770
What'll happen to us when we get there?!

01:01:09.450 --> 01:01:13.150
Neverland is said to be a world
where time stands still.

01:01:13.540 --> 01:01:16.150
A world where you can stay
the way you are forever.

01:01:17.000 --> 01:01:20.080
What'll it be? Will you
kill us and take Eureka,

01:01:20.080 --> 01:01:23.160
who might die at any time,
and fight off the entire world?

01:01:23.700 --> 01:01:26.040
Or will you come with us?

01:01:33.700 --> 01:01:35.920
Nirvash calling the Gekko.

01:01:35.920 --> 01:01:37.750
We have a deal.

01:01:37.750 --> 01:01:41.880
Renton Thurston and Eureka will
hereby join forces with the Gekko.

01:01:49.330 --> 01:01:51.060
Wait a minute! Where are you going?!

01:01:51.060 --> 01:01:52.830
Renton! Why are you leaving?!

01:01:52.830 --> 01:01:54.420
I knew I couldn't trust you!

01:01:55.450 --> 01:01:56.440
We're going on a date.

01:01:57.290 --> 01:01:59.660
--C-Come again?
--A date! A date!

01:01:59.660 --> 01:02:02.360
Geez, haven't you ever
heard of a date before?!

01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:05.370
--What are you think--
--We'll be back in 30 minutes.

01:02:05.370 --> 01:02:08.720
I'll leave my IKF running. Satisfied?

01:02:09.200 --> 01:02:10.490
Over and out.

01:02:11.450 --> 01:02:13.370
Hey! Wait a minute!

01:02:13.370 --> 01:02:14.250
Renton!

01:02:14.250 --> 01:02:16.360
Oh, what's the harm in
letting him have a little fun?

01:02:17.080 --> 01:02:21.120
Unlike you two, they've been
kept apart for years.

01:02:21.120 --> 01:02:22.390
Isn't that right, Talho?

01:02:23.290 --> 01:02:24.630
Talho? When did you--

01:02:25.290 --> 01:02:29.970
We've been deceiving the boy all this time.
I say we give him some slack.

01:02:30.540 --> 01:02:34.940
And besides... You're just mad
because you're jealous.

01:02:38.080 --> 01:02:41.440
We're not really all that different,
those people and me.

01:02:42.700 --> 01:02:49.280
Just like they turned rebel for a cause
they believed in and killed a lot of people,

01:02:49.660 --> 01:02:52.910
I've also taken lives for
something that I believe in.

01:02:54.160 --> 01:02:57.330
And it's not just people.
I've killed lots of EIZO, too.

01:02:58.290 --> 01:03:02.320
Will I end up killing a lot more
people before this is over...?

01:03:03.790 --> 01:03:06.300
Why did all this happen? How did we get here?

01:03:06.870 --> 01:03:09.500
How did things come to this?

01:03:10.870 --> 01:03:14.700
I wish we could have stayed the
way we were in Warsaw forever.

01:03:15.620 --> 01:03:17.810
I'm glad we grew up.

01:03:18.660 --> 01:03:22.030
It was because you grew up
that you came to get me.

01:03:22.950 --> 01:03:26.820
And because I grew up, I... I...

01:03:27.790 --> 01:03:30.040
I want to live.

01:03:30.040 --> 01:03:33.000
Even if it's a fake life,
I want to keep living it.

01:03:34.330 --> 01:03:36.200
Along with you, Renton.

01:03:38.120 --> 01:03:39.180
Eureka.

01:03:39.950 --> 01:03:40.840
Yes?

01:03:41.790 --> 01:03:43.450
Check it out, no hands.

01:03:57.040 --> 01:03:59.450
Idiot! Idiot! Idiot! Renton,
you're such an idiot!

01:03:59.450 --> 01:04:03.500
You scared me half to death!
I'm serious, I was terrified!

01:04:03.500 --> 01:04:04.990
Stay with me.

01:04:05.610 --> 01:04:09.990
With you at my side, I can take on anything.

01:04:10.200 --> 01:04:11.730
That's how I feel.

01:04:17.750 --> 01:04:19.130
Do me a favor.

01:04:20.590 --> 01:04:24.420
I want to take a nap together,
just like we did when we were little.

01:04:36.250 --> 01:04:39.730
Sigma 01 calling Sigma 02.
Requesting clarification.

01:04:39.730 --> 01:04:41.610
What do you mean their
controls aren't responding?

01:04:41.700 --> 01:04:44.410
This is Sigma 02. I don't know.

01:04:44.410 --> 01:04:49.500
Lambda Squad went silent right after they
called in from up ahead with that complaint.

01:04:49.500 --> 01:04:50.750
Acknowledged.

01:04:50.750 --> 01:04:52.320
Sigma 01 calling HQ.

01:04:52.580 --> 01:04:56.700
Unable to ascertain cause of Lambda,
Zeta, and Omega Squads' disappearance.

01:04:56.700 --> 01:04:58.540
Request permission for squad to withdraw.

01:04:58.540 --> 01:05:02.580
This is HQ. Acknowledged.
Permission granted to retreat to line 6-7-0-0.

01:05:02.580 --> 01:05:03.380
Roger.

01:05:03.880 --> 01:05:05.660
All units, abort search.

01:05:05.660 --> 01:05:07.750
Begin withdrawal to line 6-7-0-0--

01:05:07.750 --> 01:05:08.590
Commander!

01:05:09.080 --> 01:05:11.640
--What is it?!
--Stellar wave detected ahead!

01:05:11.640 --> 01:05:13.470
--It's closing in!
--Is it the EIZO?!

01:05:13.580 --> 01:05:16.500
No, sir! I'm getting an IKF! It's a Lambda--

01:05:16.500 --> 01:05:18.810
No, wait! What the hell is that?!

01:05:21.250 --> 01:05:23.460
--What's wrong? What happened?!
--What?! What was that?!

01:05:26.450 --> 01:05:28.200
What's wrong, Sigma 03? What happened?!

01:05:28.200 --> 01:05:29.740
I-It's no use, Commander!

01:05:29.740 --> 01:05:30.800
What's wrong, 02?!

01:05:30.800 --> 01:05:31.990
My Archetype, it's--

01:05:33.750 --> 01:05:36.620
HQ calling Sigma 01. What's happening?

01:05:36.620 --> 01:05:39.160
We're losing your IKF signals.

01:05:39.160 --> 01:05:41.950
It's no use, my Archetype
isn't responding to--

01:05:42.950 --> 01:05:46.120
What's wrong, 01?! Sigma 01, come in!

01:05:46.120 --> 01:05:47.360
Sigma 01!

01:05:53.120 --> 01:05:56.350
So, do you think his heart's in this?

01:05:56.350 --> 01:05:58.330
Whose heart is in what?

01:05:58.330 --> 01:05:59.520
Holland.

01:05:59.520 --> 01:06:00.640
What about him?

01:06:00.700 --> 01:06:04.860
Maybe he's had a change of heart
after seeing his lady collapse.

01:06:04.860 --> 01:06:08.000
Renton gets a lock on us,
and Holland gives them

01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:11.580
free run of the ship without
any punishment at all.

01:06:11.580 --> 01:06:15.450
You saw that, right? You saw
how the Nirvash could fight.

01:06:15.750 --> 01:06:18.250
In the myth, the White Sacred One

01:06:18.250 --> 01:06:21.370
is supposed to purify its
enemies without fighting.

01:06:21.620 --> 01:06:24.710
But that thing engaged
a whole damn army flotilla.

01:06:24.710 --> 01:06:25.720
Why'd it do that?

01:06:26.300 --> 01:06:31.450
W-Wait a minute, you're not
saying they're fakes, are you?

01:06:31.450 --> 01:06:35.180
I don't want to believe it,
but maybe we've been had.

01:06:35.450 --> 01:06:38.250
Been had? By what?

01:06:38.250 --> 01:06:42.410
We stole Eureka on the assumption
that she was the army's top-secret item.

01:06:42.410 --> 01:06:46.700
But what if the thing we
recovered wasn't the real Eureka?

01:06:47.290 --> 01:06:50.750
And what if Holland knew about it?

01:06:50.750 --> 01:06:52.120
What're you getting at?

01:06:52.120 --> 01:06:53.870
Take a close look at this.

01:06:53.870 --> 01:06:56.280
This picture is based off of
what's in the Ageha Myth.

01:06:57.370 --> 01:07:01.830
The maiden in the myth had wings on her back.

01:07:01.830 --> 01:07:05.540
She saves the land and guides lost souls,
and to prove her identity, she has--

01:07:05.540 --> 01:07:08.320
Wait a minute. Eureka doesn't have...

01:07:09.000 --> 01:07:10.920
We can't trust Holland anymore.

01:07:10.920 --> 01:07:14.660
Which is why I say we have to check this out.

01:07:14.660 --> 01:07:16.050
Personally.

01:07:17.200 --> 01:07:20.680
About these unexplained KLF runaways...

01:07:20.830 --> 01:07:25.540
According to the army, there is
absolutely no way to counteract it!

01:07:25.540 --> 01:07:31.890
Surely you know that we cannot hold
the EIZO in check without KLFs!

01:07:32.330 --> 01:07:34.410
How much time do we have?

01:07:34.410 --> 01:07:35.790
None at all!

01:07:36.660 --> 01:07:40.790
Look at this. KLF runaways
have already been confirmed

01:07:40.790 --> 01:07:43.700
in 80% of human-controlled territory.

01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:48.420
And in spite of this, you <i>still </i>have
qualms about firing the Hammer of God?

01:07:49.250 --> 01:07:50.580
I am frightened.

01:07:50.580 --> 01:07:51.910
Frightened?!

01:07:51.910 --> 01:07:58.030
Surely you know that the world will be
buried in ash from the Hammer of God.

01:07:58.660 --> 01:08:03.020
Is wounding our own mother planet
an action that we should take...?

01:08:03.230 --> 01:08:07.140
Perhaps that sentimentality
is what cost you your marriage.

01:08:08.020 --> 01:08:10.000
Ah, my apologies.

01:08:10.000 --> 01:08:14.750
In any event, we chosen people
will be safe on the escape ship.

01:08:14.750 --> 01:08:18.030
We hope you will make the wise decision.

01:08:22.700 --> 01:08:24.540
Too sentimental, am I?

01:08:24.970 --> 01:08:28.620
Would an overly sentimental
man send his own ex-wife

01:08:28.620 --> 01:08:31.920
scrambling around on a million-to-one
longshot investigation?

01:08:31.920 --> 01:08:33.400
"Myth Regeneration Project"

01:08:33.400 --> 01:08:35.550
On an investigation for hope...
"Myth Regeneration Project"

01:08:35.550 --> 01:08:36.830
"Myth Regeneration Project"

01:08:36.830 --> 01:08:37.220
Minister Coda, just as you said,
"Myth Regeneration Project"

01:08:37.220 --> 01:08:39.150
"Playing"
Minister Coda, just as you said,

01:08:39.150 --> 01:08:41.260
we've confirmed that the boy
"Playing"

01:08:41.260 --> 01:08:46.850
named Renton Thurston is the son of the
Warsaw cult group's technical supervisor.

01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:52.330
Evidence suggests that this
girl-shaped EIZO was being raised

01:08:52.330 --> 01:08:55.620
alongside this boy that we
believe was the same age.

01:08:56.330 --> 01:08:59.120
Going from the few remaining records,

01:08:59.120 --> 01:09:02.780
it seems that the cultists were
always recording their dreams.

01:09:02.780 --> 01:09:04.500
Recording their dreams?

01:09:04.500 --> 01:09:05.500
Yes, ma'am.

01:09:05.500 --> 01:09:09.510
And judging from those recordings,
I'm led to believe that their experiments

01:09:09.510 --> 01:09:12.600
were meant to cause the boy
and girl to share their dreams.

01:09:13.580 --> 01:09:18.910
Or rather, to cause the girl to have
the same dream that the boy was having.

01:09:21.580 --> 01:09:23.430
I don't believe it...
Shouldn't that be impossible?

01:09:23.700 --> 01:09:26.220
Perhaps, but all the pieces fit.

01:09:26.590 --> 01:09:31.620
It's safe to assume that the
Children of Neverland are trying to use

01:09:31.620 --> 01:09:37.290
the Thurston boy and the secret item
Eureka to create their ideal world.

01:09:37.910 --> 01:09:42.670
Perhaps their goal is a world
where time stands still.

01:09:43.210 --> 01:09:47.260
After all, they <i>are </i>aging several
times faster than normal.

01:09:47.660 --> 01:09:49.330
Just a minute, ma'am...

01:09:49.750 --> 01:09:54.620
When the Tragedy of Doha happened,
they were using 4 terawatts of energy.

01:09:54.620 --> 01:09:58.720
That's as much power as a country uses.
Where would they get it?

01:09:59.340 --> 01:10:01.160
They don't need to go out and find it.

01:10:02.160 --> 01:10:04.720
They just need to jump into it.

01:10:05.200 --> 01:10:07.290
Into the energy of the Hammer of God.

01:10:08.410 --> 01:10:12.410
If we don't fire the Hammer of God,
humanity will be wiped out.

01:10:12.410 --> 01:10:16.650
But if we <i>do </i>fire it, we'll have
a repeat of the Tragedy of Doha.

01:10:17.540 --> 01:10:20.400
Humanity is between a
rock and a hard place...

01:10:28.330 --> 01:10:29.500
Did you see anything?

01:10:30.790 --> 01:10:31.870
Sorry.

01:10:31.870 --> 01:10:33.010
Oh.

01:10:33.670 --> 01:10:36.410
I bet it's because we were apart for so long.

01:10:37.660 --> 01:10:38.700
Tell me.

01:10:38.700 --> 01:10:39.870
What?

01:10:39.870 --> 01:10:43.800
Do you really trust the people on this ship?

01:10:44.700 --> 01:10:50.170
Didn't I tell you? I'll fight the people
on this ship, humanity, and the EIZO.

01:10:50.750 --> 01:10:54.410
The only things I believe in
are you and Nirvash.

01:11:06.120 --> 01:11:07.450
E-Eureka!

01:11:08.040 --> 01:11:12.170
I-I'm sorry! I didn't mean--
where are you going?

01:11:12.170 --> 01:11:14.460
Sheesh, don't ask me that!

01:11:14.620 --> 01:11:19.130
To the bathroom! Even robots made
by the EIZO go to the bathroom!

01:11:23.250 --> 01:11:27.260
Sheesh, I didn't think Renton
would be so short on tact.

01:11:43.870 --> 01:11:44.860
What was...

01:11:47.780 --> 01:11:49.830
What's wrong? What are these tremors?

01:11:49.830 --> 01:11:52.620
It's not an external attack!
It's coming from inside!

01:11:52.620 --> 01:11:53.870
They're from inside the ship!

01:11:53.870 --> 01:11:54.950
They're what?!

01:11:54.950 --> 01:11:57.000
Stellar waves detected in hangar!

01:11:57.000 --> 01:11:57.620
What?!

01:11:57.620 --> 01:11:59.920
Stellar waves detected from all KLFs...

01:11:59.920 --> 01:12:03.090
It's no use! The Archetypes
can't maintain their shapes!

01:12:05.120 --> 01:12:06.120
This is bad...

01:12:06.830 --> 01:12:10.980
Vent the air from all hangars! The low
oxygen will knock out the Archetypes!

01:12:10.980 --> 01:12:14.560
I can't! I'm reading one
lifesign in hangar ♪1!

01:12:14.560 --> 01:12:17.630
Wait a minute... It's... It's Eureka!

01:12:17.630 --> 01:12:21.070
Nirvash! Please, Nirvash! Stop this!

01:12:24.500 --> 01:12:26.750
Why? Why are you doing this, Nirvash?

01:12:26.750 --> 01:12:29.630
You don't have to react to this!

01:12:29.630 --> 01:12:32.240
Bridge calling all crew! Somebody, anybody!

01:12:32.240 --> 01:12:36.330
Get down to the hangar and pull
Eureka away from the KLFs!

01:12:40.200 --> 01:12:42.860
Nirvash! Nirvash!

01:12:43.580 --> 01:12:44.590
Renton?

01:12:45.540 --> 01:12:47.310
What the hell?

01:12:48.580 --> 01:12:52.200
You little bitch! What are you doing?!
Stop him right now!

01:12:52.200 --> 01:12:55.290
Stop him how? I can't do that!

01:12:55.290 --> 01:12:56.790
Bullshit!

01:12:58.410 --> 01:13:02.690
Or maybe you're right.
Maybe you really can't stop him.

01:13:03.750 --> 01:13:07.840
You're not really the top
secret item, <i>are </i>you?

01:13:08.410 --> 01:13:11.790
How long have you been at it?
How long have you been tricking humans?

01:13:11.790 --> 01:13:13.700
No! No!

01:13:13.700 --> 01:13:15.540
Now, now, quit fighting!

01:13:15.540 --> 01:13:18.410
Like a fake human needs any modesty!

01:13:23.910 --> 01:13:24.950
What's...

01:13:26.000 --> 01:13:27.190
Nirvash!

01:13:33.870 --> 01:13:35.220
Just like I thought.

01:13:35.700 --> 01:13:39.620
Crap! We were duped by a fake?

01:13:39.620 --> 01:13:42.250
This proves it. Holland was--

01:13:42.250 --> 01:13:43.950
Bastard!

01:13:43.950 --> 01:13:46.450
What did you do to Eureka?!

01:13:48.250 --> 01:13:50.530
--Son of a bitch!
- -Cut it out!

01:13:51.830 --> 01:13:53.990
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

01:13:53.990 --> 01:13:57.370
--I'll kill anybody who hurts Eureka!
--Stop it!

01:13:57.450 --> 01:14:00.030
Stop, damn it! Stop!!

01:14:08.120 --> 01:14:09.260
What happened here?

01:14:10.790 --> 01:14:11.870
Hap!

01:14:12.660 --> 01:14:15.250
What happened here?! How are the KLFs?!

01:14:15.250 --> 01:14:16.470
It wasn't my fault.

01:14:17.160 --> 01:14:18.270
It wasn't my--

01:14:24.940 --> 01:14:26.080
Hap?

01:14:34.910 --> 01:14:35.780
That's...

01:14:47.130 --> 01:14:50.130
Nooo!!

01:14:53.290 --> 01:14:56.620
The firing can no longer be stopped?
Is that what you're saying?

01:14:56.620 --> 01:14:57.830
Yes.

01:14:57.830 --> 01:15:02.060
Even if the resulting repeat of the Tragedy
of Doha annihilates the solar system?

01:15:02.060 --> 01:15:05.450
The whole galaxy?

01:15:05.450 --> 01:15:09.940
A country can't operate on
speculation. Look at this footage.

01:15:10.660 --> 01:15:11.750
What's this?

01:15:11.750 --> 01:15:17.330
Fourteen hours ago, EIZO worldwide
began assembling in Antarctica.

01:15:17.330 --> 01:15:23.040
The timing coincides with the
destruction of KLFs around the world.

01:15:23.950 --> 01:15:26.540
They're preparing for a final battle, too?

01:15:26.540 --> 01:15:31.160
Our calculations show that if we fire
the Hammer of God at full power,

01:15:31.160 --> 01:15:33.560
we can annihilate them all in one blast.

01:15:34.500 --> 01:15:36.540
So it's too late...

01:15:37.540 --> 01:15:39.900
I have a high-speed aircraft standing by.

01:15:40.640 --> 01:15:44.140
Show them your ticket, and they
will take you to the spaceport.

01:15:45.370 --> 01:15:48.700
Bear witness to the future in my place.

01:15:50.080 --> 01:15:56.480
If you and I had kids, I expect you would
be saying those words to someone else.

01:15:58.580 --> 01:16:00.070
I suppose I would.

01:16:01.660 --> 01:16:04.700
So, are you feeling better now?

01:16:04.700 --> 01:16:06.080
Yes, I'm fine.

01:16:06.080 --> 01:16:07.580
That's good.

01:16:07.580 --> 01:16:11.910
I heard what happened to Renton.
The next three days will be critical.

01:16:12.670 --> 01:16:15.170
Looks like our luck hasn't quite run out yet.

01:16:16.160 --> 01:16:18.970
The Hammer of God will fire in twelve hours.

01:16:19.450 --> 01:16:23.390
If we can do something with Nirvash in his
larval state, we might still pull this off.

01:16:26.370 --> 01:16:31.910
If we make it there, will we
really be happy in Neverland?

01:16:31.910 --> 01:16:35.990
Who's to say? But if we don't go,
we've got no future.

01:16:36.290 --> 01:16:40.190
Tell me, Holland. What's the future to you?

01:16:40.830 --> 01:16:42.030
My future...

01:16:43.010 --> 01:16:44.370
is you.

01:16:44.910 --> 01:16:50.110
A world that you're in. The future
that you want. That's my future.

01:16:50.540 --> 01:16:52.100
I don't need anything else.

01:16:53.200 --> 01:16:55.640
Holland, I need to tell you something...

01:16:57.790 --> 01:17:02.010
We need you on the bridge, Holland.
We're about to start our landing approach.

01:17:02.620 --> 01:17:03.890
We're here.

01:17:04.450 --> 01:17:07.160
We made it to the pink-haired woman's place.

01:17:26.540 --> 01:17:31.000
Things are the other way around, huh?
This is all my fault, isn't it?

01:17:31.830 --> 01:17:34.000
I'm sorry, Renton.

01:17:35.000 --> 01:17:39.730
But because of this, I finally
understand how you feel, Renton.

01:17:40.700 --> 01:17:45.510
How you felt when you came
to see me when I was locked up.

01:17:46.160 --> 01:17:50.100
How you felt when you
came to save me in Nirvash.

01:17:51.200 --> 01:17:54.720
I love you, Renton. I love you so much.

01:17:56.120 --> 01:17:58.190
So please, don't die...

01:18:01.580 --> 01:18:03.790
No, I won't let you die.

01:18:03.790 --> 01:18:08.410
I don't know if I can be
as brave as you, Renton...

01:18:08.410 --> 01:18:10.580
...but I won't let you die.

01:18:14.120 --> 01:18:16.300
Thank you, Nirvash.

01:18:21.520 --> 01:18:24.160
I might be a failure as
your secretary, ma'am.

01:18:24.160 --> 01:18:29.460
I'm unable to stick with you to the bitter end,
and you've even given me your ticket.

01:18:30.200 --> 01:18:35.090
It's all right. You've done more
than enough for me, Maria.

01:18:36.330 --> 01:18:39.040
You're going to where No. 6
is being kept, aren't you?

01:18:39.040 --> 01:18:41.090
I have to see this through.

01:18:41.090 --> 01:18:44.770
I'll keep digging at the truth
right up to the end of the world.

01:18:45.410 --> 01:18:49.910
Even if I don't catch up with No. 7
or the Children of Neverland.

01:18:49.910 --> 01:18:51.580
You're a formidable woman.

01:18:51.580 --> 01:18:53.460
No, I just don't know when to give up.

01:18:54.160 --> 01:18:55.270
And besides...

01:18:58.200 --> 01:18:59.750
I should go.

01:19:00.790 --> 01:19:02.180
May God watch over you.

01:19:02.840 --> 01:19:06.280
Give Jurgens... Give your husband my regards.

01:19:06.790 --> 01:19:08.430
Be happy together.

01:19:10.660 --> 01:19:11.850
We will!

01:19:22.620 --> 01:19:26.490
Apparently, they built No. 6's
containment facility here,

01:19:26.490 --> 01:19:29.160
700 meters below the
abandoned Vodarac Shrine,

01:19:29.160 --> 01:19:34.970
to keep her from being detected
by EIZO interference waves.

01:19:36.320 --> 01:19:40.000
That's how afraid they were
of No. 6's abilities, eh?

01:19:40.580 --> 01:19:43.830
They were afraid of having a
repeat of the Tragedy of Doha.

01:19:43.830 --> 01:19:46.860
I didn't expect it to be so massive.

01:19:47.200 --> 01:19:49.640
I'm actually speechless for once.

01:19:49.870 --> 01:19:52.290
--Confirm we've stopped. Holland.
--What the--?

01:19:52.290 --> 01:19:54.690
Got it. Lower the catapult.

01:19:55.250 --> 01:19:56.190
We're going ashore.

01:19:56.190 --> 01:19:58.310
Wait a minute! There's somebody up ahead!

01:19:58.310 --> 01:19:59.830
No way! Is it the army?!

01:19:59.830 --> 01:20:01.300
I'm putting it up on the screen!

01:20:05.120 --> 01:20:08.160
Who... Who is that?

01:20:08.160 --> 01:20:10.030
Holland, you don't suppose it's--

01:20:10.700 --> 01:20:12.720
It's Prof. Dominic's fiancée.

01:20:13.160 --> 01:20:14.500
His fiancée?

01:20:14.500 --> 01:20:17.920
She's the being that you
humans designated No. 6.

01:20:18.240 --> 01:20:22.700
I can tell. It's because that
person is the same as me.

01:20:22.700 --> 01:20:25.720
That's the woman that Prof. Dominic loved.

01:20:26.120 --> 01:20:27.300
Anemone.

01:20:29.200 --> 01:20:31.940
I finally get to meet all those children.

01:20:32.910 --> 01:20:34.970
But I wasn't able to get everything ready.

01:20:37.070 --> 01:20:37.900
That's true.

01:20:39.410 --> 01:20:42.410
I was able to finish this,
so he'll forgive us, won't he?

01:20:43.410 --> 01:20:47.280
This is where it all begins.
But will the children

01:20:47.280 --> 01:20:47.780
"New World Myth"
This is where it all begins.
But will the children

01:20:47.780 --> 01:20:49.780
be happy about it, I wonder?
"New World Myth"

01:20:50.660 --> 01:20:53.580
The Hammer of God has entered planned area.

01:20:53.580 --> 01:20:56.500
Primary mechanism is
currently running at 85%.

01:20:56.500 --> 01:20:58.040
And the ancillary mechanisms?

01:20:58.040 --> 01:21:00.170
Time to deployment completion: 2 hours.

01:21:00.170 --> 01:21:03.800
Operation schedule is on time.
All systems are running smoothly.

01:21:04.080 --> 01:21:05.440
That's good.

01:21:05.870 --> 01:21:07.880
Still, look at that core...

01:21:08.210 --> 01:21:11.460
It's as if it's made the land
itself into a plant nursery bed.

01:21:11.910 --> 01:21:15.370
Just like a flower of this world...

01:21:16.370 --> 01:21:18.200
EIZO interference wave detected!

01:21:18.200 --> 01:21:22.950
Magnitude: level 9!
Bearing: 080 by 225 by 11!

01:21:22.950 --> 01:21:25.230
Point of emanation:
Vodarac autonomous region!

01:21:25.230 --> 01:21:27.160
The Vodarac autonomous region?!

01:21:27.160 --> 01:21:28.910
Is it targeting No. 6?

01:21:28.910 --> 01:21:33.250
Or... Does this mean that
No. 7 has arrived there?!

01:21:33.830 --> 01:21:35.450
What are you doing there?

01:21:36.040 --> 01:21:39.460
It's almost as if you knew
we were coming, Anemone.

01:21:40.080 --> 01:21:43.460
There is so much I want to explain,
but there is no time.

01:21:44.250 --> 01:21:47.080
Thank you for all your help, The End.

01:21:48.160 --> 01:21:50.810
That's right. Please look after them.

01:21:57.620 --> 01:21:59.080
What's your game?

01:21:59.080 --> 01:22:01.160
I gave Dominic my word.

01:22:01.160 --> 01:22:02.230
Your word?

01:22:02.910 --> 01:22:08.030
If those who appeared before me were
without hope, the seal would remain.

01:22:08.540 --> 01:22:11.090
But if those who appeared did have hope,

01:22:11.820 --> 01:22:14.330
I would release the seal
for the sake of their wishes.

01:22:14.330 --> 01:22:18.660
Then, when the White Sacred
One appeared, I would aid them

01:22:18.660 --> 01:22:22.290
and transform their hope into
a road that leads to the future.

01:22:31.830 --> 01:22:34.200
What the--? What are these tremors?

01:22:34.200 --> 01:22:36.660
--I don't believe it...
--The EIZO!

01:22:38.080 --> 01:22:39.090
Gidget!

01:22:39.410 --> 01:22:42.290
Ow... Huh? My gun!

01:22:42.290 --> 01:22:44.310
Take Renton to a hospital!

01:22:44.450 --> 01:22:46.500
Eureka, what are--

01:22:46.500 --> 01:22:48.330
Didn't you hear me?

01:22:48.330 --> 01:22:52.740
I told you to start up
the Gekko and take Renton to a hospital!

01:22:53.790 --> 01:22:57.000
Don't make me any angrier than I already am.

01:23:25.790 --> 01:23:28.790
What's all the racket...? Ow...

01:23:31.080 --> 01:23:32.420
Professor!

01:23:32.910 --> 01:23:35.060
It's been a long time, Renton.

01:23:36.250 --> 01:23:37.750
Calm down, Eureka!

01:23:37.750 --> 01:23:41.500
Even if we took Renton to a doctor,
there's no guarantee he could save him!

01:23:41.500 --> 01:23:43.390
You're better off coming with us, so--

01:23:43.390 --> 01:23:44.660
Not a chance!

01:23:44.660 --> 01:23:45.710
Eureka?

01:23:45.950 --> 01:23:49.090
My whole life, I've done
nothing but run away.

01:23:49.330 --> 01:23:53.640
I'd always run away, using my
mission or my fate as excuses!

01:23:54.620 --> 01:23:58.550
But I'm through with running. I'll fight.

01:23:58.910 --> 01:24:01.900
Just like Renton has always done for me.

01:24:03.040 --> 01:24:05.060
For the future that I want to see happen!

01:24:19.910 --> 01:24:21.700
You're ready, I see.

01:24:27.290 --> 01:24:29.830
Professor, I'm sorry.

01:24:29.830 --> 01:24:30.880
Why are you apologizing?

01:24:31.410 --> 01:24:34.380
Because it doesn't look like
I'll be able to keep my promise.

01:24:34.910 --> 01:24:35.880
Why not?

01:24:36.450 --> 01:24:39.330
Look at me--my body won't move.

01:24:39.330 --> 01:24:42.560
No matter how much I order it to
move with my mind, it won't listen.

01:24:43.480 --> 01:24:44.830
Why? Why does this happen?

01:24:44.830 --> 01:24:49.380
Why does my body always
freeze up when I need it the most?

01:24:50.290 --> 01:24:52.470
You're still thinking with your head?

01:24:54.300 --> 01:24:58.330
That's what you've learned in
these past eight years, Renton?

01:24:59.500 --> 01:25:05.200
Say, do you know the real reason
that we can't have dreams?

01:25:05.910 --> 01:25:10.370
The reason is that we ourselves are dreams.

01:25:11.450 --> 01:25:17.000
We're imaginary beings that were created
by the EIZO in response to human dreams.

01:25:17.700 --> 01:25:20.520
That's why Dominic halted the experiments.

01:25:21.290 --> 01:25:23.850
Because he didn't want me to disappear.

01:25:24.830 --> 01:25:27.870
I don't know where the EIZO came from.

01:25:27.870 --> 01:25:30.410
And I don't know what
they're trying to accomplish.

01:25:30.410 --> 01:25:33.440
But there is one thing
that I can say for certain.

01:25:33.440 --> 01:25:36.940
Even if humanity makes contact with the EIZO,
dreams are nothing but dreams.

01:25:37.580 --> 01:25:40.330
Reality can only be changed by reality.

01:25:40.330 --> 01:25:45.210
Wait a minute! If that's true,
why do you and I exist here?

01:25:45.950 --> 01:25:47.330
Humans are foolish.

01:25:48.250 --> 01:25:53.460
Their shallow imagination nipped
their hope for the future in the bud.

01:25:53.660 --> 01:25:55.570
And this world is the result.

01:25:56.250 --> 01:25:58.240
Do you see it, Renton?

01:25:59.250 --> 01:26:00.730
The EIZO are a mirror.

01:26:01.210 --> 01:26:05.330
A mirror that reflects the true
nature of what's in front of it.

01:26:05.330 --> 01:26:07.250
I don't know the reason why.

01:26:07.250 --> 01:26:11.500
But you, I, even the EIZO, are alive.

01:26:11.500 --> 01:26:12.960
Through no choice of our own.

01:26:13.480 --> 01:26:18.370
Forced to be alive as part of this world
that's so full of fear and anger.

01:26:18.370 --> 01:26:22.000
Our deaths would spell
the death of this world itself.

01:26:22.620 --> 01:26:27.630
Wait a minute! No! If that's true,
then what am I supposed to do?

01:26:28.200 --> 01:26:30.290
You're ready now, right?

01:26:31.290 --> 01:26:33.240
Ready to have a dream of your own.

01:26:33.830 --> 01:26:36.170
Professor, I don't understand...

01:26:36.620 --> 01:26:38.130
What should I do?

01:26:38.580 --> 01:26:40.870
Please, Professor, tell me!

01:26:40.870 --> 01:26:42.540
You already know.

01:26:43.870 --> 01:26:46.110
Not up here, but in here.

01:26:49.580 --> 01:26:52.220
Ah. My time is up.

01:26:53.410 --> 01:26:56.150
Professor, where are you going? Professor!

01:26:56.330 --> 01:26:57.530
Professor!

01:26:58.450 --> 01:27:01.700
I love your rough and tumble way of living.

01:27:02.040 --> 01:27:06.280
So I'll leave you some parting words
that should help you with that.

01:27:06.830 --> 01:27:07.920
They're...

01:27:08.700 --> 01:27:10.000
Professor...!

01:27:10.000 --> 01:27:12.290
Professor! Professor!

01:27:12.290 --> 01:27:14.200
Professor!

01:27:22.410 --> 01:27:26.660
I heard him... I heard his last words.

01:27:33.230 --> 01:27:34.420
Don't beg for it!

01:27:34.830 --> 01:27:38.650
Don't beg for it, earn it!
Then it will be granted to you!

01:27:42.000 --> 01:27:42.780
Oh, crap!

01:27:45.200 --> 01:27:46.220
Save me...

01:27:46.750 --> 01:27:48.500
Save me, Renton!

01:27:52.500 --> 01:27:53.160
He's here.

01:28:05.040 --> 01:28:08.370
What the--? What the hell is that?!

01:28:10.910 --> 01:28:14.790
I don't believe it... Is that you? Nirvash?

01:28:16.080 --> 01:28:17.020
Nirvash!

01:28:46.250 --> 01:28:47.750
Eureka!

01:28:50.540 --> 01:28:57.240
I'm sorry, Eureka. I might not have the
means or the courage to protect you yet.

01:28:57.580 --> 01:29:00.250
But the Professor told me!

01:29:00.250 --> 01:29:03.530
I want to win the future with you, Eureka!

01:29:04.330 --> 01:29:08.080
So let's go together, Eureka!

01:29:08.080 --> 01:29:10.410
I love you!

01:29:11.580 --> 01:29:12.520
Renton...

01:29:13.040 --> 01:29:15.620
Renton! Renton!

01:29:19.540 --> 01:29:20.390
Holland!

01:29:21.450 --> 01:29:23.700
"One shall transcend the limits of the world.

01:29:23.700 --> 01:29:23.710
When the voice of his
body and soul rings out,
"One shall transcend the limits of the world.

01:29:23.710 --> 01:29:25.950
When the voice of his
body and soul rings out,

01:29:25.950 --> 01:29:28.250
the two children shall become one,

01:29:28.250 --> 01:29:30.690
and they shall become the White Sacred One."

01:29:31.830 --> 01:29:33.720
What happened to you?!

01:29:34.290 --> 01:29:36.750
What did you do?!

01:29:36.750 --> 01:29:39.910
What did I do? I gave them
some encouragement, that's all.

01:29:39.910 --> 01:29:44.040
If we don't reenact the myth, we're all dead!
You knew that, and you still--

01:29:44.040 --> 01:29:45.860
--You're a spoiled baby.
--What?

01:29:46.250 --> 01:29:49.280
Why didn't you even bother to try
to create a myth of your own?

01:29:50.040 --> 01:29:51.590
Like those two did.

01:29:52.080 --> 01:29:53.370
No way.

01:29:53.370 --> 01:29:58.250
This is the result of those two
refusing to reenact the myth?

01:29:59.700 --> 01:30:02.090
--Oh, wow...
- -It's beautiful.

01:30:02.700 --> 01:30:05.370
Now, off you go! To the future!

01:30:13.620 --> 01:30:15.200
It's getting away...

01:30:15.200 --> 01:30:18.390
Our dreams. Our future...

01:30:19.250 --> 01:30:20.580
I won't let you.

01:30:20.580 --> 01:30:23.650
I am <i>not </i>gonna let you do this!

01:30:30.080 --> 01:30:34.910
Long ago, it was believed that
the sun was a supreme being

01:30:34.910 --> 01:30:39.750
that bestowed limitless energy
which never needed to be repaid.

01:30:41.040 --> 01:30:47.090
This provided a rationale to humanity
for their excess and consumption.

01:30:47.580 --> 01:30:51.700
And to prove this, humanity
created the human sacrifice,

01:30:51.700 --> 01:30:54.450
whose heart was offered up to the gods.

01:30:54.450 --> 01:30:56.550
Oh, the irony.

01:30:57.390 --> 01:31:00.580
We are no different from the ancients.

01:31:00.580 --> 01:31:06.410
We harness the sun's energy and
use it as a weapon to burn invaders.

01:31:06.410 --> 01:31:11.740
What can one call this, if not the
ultimate in excess and consumption?

01:31:12.080 --> 01:31:14.660
May our posterity forgive us.

01:31:14.660 --> 01:31:18.990
Having tasted the pleasure of consumption,
we are unable to stop ourselves.

01:31:19.320 --> 01:31:22.800
Operation: Hammer of God... Initiate!

01:31:57.500 --> 01:32:00.700
Rays have reached primary mechanism!
Countdown commencing!

01:32:00.700 --> 01:32:05.240
T-minus 1246 seconds!
Observation teams, relay info as needed!

01:32:05.830 --> 01:32:07.250
You idiot.

01:32:08.000 --> 01:32:09.660
Renton, you're such an idiot.

01:32:10.240 --> 01:32:13.690
As hurt as you are, you might die...

01:32:14.160 --> 01:32:16.830
What on earth were you thinking, you idiot?

01:32:16.830 --> 01:32:18.540
Stop calling me an idiot all the time.

01:32:19.420 --> 01:32:22.330
It's not like I can help it.
I <i>am </i>an idiot, after all.

01:32:22.830 --> 01:32:26.700
But I can't be an idiot
for anyone but you, Eureka.

01:32:28.370 --> 01:32:29.330
Idiot.

01:32:29.750 --> 01:32:32.770
But you're my idiot.

01:32:35.040 --> 01:32:35.870
So...

01:32:36.410 --> 01:32:37.260
Yeah?

01:32:37.260 --> 01:32:40.450
Where do we go from here?

01:32:40.700 --> 01:32:42.300
Where do you want to go?

01:32:42.970 --> 01:32:44.620
Anywhere is fine.

01:32:45.250 --> 01:32:49.850
As long as you're there, Renton,
I don't care where we go.

01:32:54.980 --> 01:32:56.260
Nirvash...

01:32:56.800 --> 01:32:58.980
Renton, what did he say?

01:32:59.290 --> 01:33:01.700
Oh. Well, he said...

01:33:07.290 --> 01:33:10.610
I'm impressed that you dodged
my fire hurt as bad as you are.

01:33:11.470 --> 01:33:16.090
I wish I could be a gentleman and
compliment you, but I'm not that mature.

01:33:16.580 --> 01:33:19.410
Listen up. I'll ask you one more time.

01:33:19.410 --> 01:33:22.080
Will you come with us?

01:33:28.440 --> 01:33:31.770
I see. So that's your answer, Renton?!

01:33:32.250 --> 01:33:34.910
It's a shame. It's a real shame.

01:33:34.910 --> 01:33:38.040
And here I thought you were
the same kind of man as me!

01:33:39.040 --> 01:33:40.770
Don't put me on your level...

01:33:40.770 --> 01:33:41.680
What?

01:33:41.680 --> 01:33:46.950
I never used people as playthings
because I'm ruled by my past!

01:33:50.250 --> 01:33:53.120
Playthings? Don't make me laugh!

01:33:53.120 --> 01:33:57.360
How are you gonna make up
for killing Hap and Stoner?!

01:33:59.410 --> 01:34:01.870
Stop trying to change the subject!

01:34:14.480 --> 01:34:15.440
Renton!

01:34:16.000 --> 01:34:18.020
You don't know anything.

01:34:18.950 --> 01:34:21.500
You think you know how I feel?

01:34:21.500 --> 01:34:24.330
How it feels to have everything
taken away from you?

01:34:24.330 --> 01:34:28.040
Losing the chance to love, talk about
your dreams, and think about the future?

01:34:28.040 --> 01:34:31.520
You couldn't possibly know how it feels!

01:34:33.500 --> 01:34:35.020
Is this true?

01:34:35.020 --> 01:34:38.940
I'm not a real doctor, so
I can't say for certain.

01:34:38.940 --> 01:34:42.790
But I feel safe in saying I'm 99% sure.

01:34:42.790 --> 01:34:44.400
Well, well.

01:34:44.400 --> 01:34:46.290
That settles it, then!

01:34:46.290 --> 01:34:49.540
Gidget! Can you get us
the 20 on that bonehead?

01:34:49.880 --> 01:34:52.750
Yeah! He's left his IKF
transmitting like a good boy!

01:34:52.750 --> 01:34:56.410
Right! Sound the alarm for all
hands to fasten their seatbelts!

01:34:56.410 --> 01:34:57.500
Aye aye!

01:34:57.500 --> 01:34:59.500
Guys... You'd do this for me?

01:34:59.500 --> 01:35:02.340
Come on, you need to buckle up, too.

01:35:02.950 --> 01:35:05.700
We're all going to hitch a ride.

01:35:05.700 --> 01:35:07.890
On the future that's inside of you.

01:35:11.220 --> 01:35:12.580
Thank you...

01:35:12.580 --> 01:35:14.750
Thank you, everybody...

01:35:15.750 --> 01:35:18.400
The radiance unleashed
by the Hammer of God...

01:35:18.910 --> 01:35:21.820
What sort of future is waiting for us?

01:35:21.820 --> 01:35:24.000
A gray purgatory? Or a world of nothingness?

01:35:24.580 --> 01:35:26.300
Good question. Who's to say?

01:35:27.440 --> 01:35:30.540
All myths are woven according
to the whims of the storyteller.

01:35:30.540 --> 01:35:35.920
And in all myths, the teller is
never a participant in the tale.

01:35:36.870 --> 01:35:39.440
You got here just in time, Madam Storyteller.

01:35:39.830 --> 01:35:41.040
No. 6!

01:35:41.040 --> 01:35:43.540
Now, shall we watch?

01:35:44.160 --> 01:35:47.790
Let's see how our new myth unfolds.

01:35:50.200 --> 01:35:53.050
It won't stop... The bleeding won't stop!

01:35:53.910 --> 01:35:58.410
No! Renton, don't fall
asleep! Renton, wake up!

01:36:03.250 --> 01:36:04.950
Come back here!

01:36:29.620 --> 01:36:30.640
Damn!

01:36:40.620 --> 01:36:44.030
I won't accept it... I'll never accept it.

01:36:44.500 --> 01:36:48.950
A life of being used, of being discarded...
A life not worth living!

01:36:48.950 --> 01:36:51.620
I'll never accept it!

01:36:51.620 --> 01:36:54.960
Compressor to maximum!
Distortion canceller disengaged!

01:36:55.290 --> 01:37:00.340
Oh, no! That fool Holland has set his
Compac Feedback System to maximum!

01:37:00.340 --> 01:37:02.290
Holland, no!

01:37:02.790 --> 01:37:04.970
Rest easy, Talho...

01:37:05.290 --> 01:37:07.910
I'll blaze a trail to the future for you.

01:37:07.910 --> 01:37:11.390
I'll bring back the White Sacred One
even if it costs me my life.

01:37:12.040 --> 01:37:15.500
So take my place and regenerate
the myth for me, guys.

01:37:15.500 --> 01:37:20.120
And protect Talho's life for me...
Protect Talho's future for me!

01:37:29.660 --> 01:37:33.220
Nirvash... Nirvash said
something to me a minute ago.

01:37:33.660 --> 01:37:36.790
He said he'd take us back to our Neverland...

01:37:38.370 --> 01:37:43.540
I wanted the two of us to
walk under Neverland's sun...

01:37:45.000 --> 01:37:49.350
But I'm sorry... I can't say
"Let's go together" this time...

01:37:49.840 --> 01:37:52.540
We will! We'll go together!

01:37:54.200 --> 01:37:56.180
Renton!

01:38:18.730 --> 01:38:20.120
Papa!

01:38:23.970 --> 01:38:25.790
Holland!

01:38:35.910 --> 01:38:40.200
Why'd you do it?
Why'd you keep it a secret, Talho?

01:38:40.200 --> 01:38:44.450
I'm sorry. But... come on, if I'd
told you, you'd have given it all up.

01:38:44.450 --> 01:38:46.900
You would have given up your own dreams.

01:38:47.230 --> 01:38:49.370
That's the kind of man you are.

01:38:50.620 --> 01:38:52.000
You want to have it, right?

01:38:53.080 --> 01:38:54.000
Yes.

01:38:55.370 --> 01:38:56.700
Don't you remember?

01:38:57.150 --> 01:39:01.170
Whatever future you want, that's my future.

01:39:01.870 --> 01:39:02.990
I'm sorry...

01:39:03.620 --> 01:39:07.250
I'm so sorry... I'm so sorry...

01:39:07.250 --> 01:39:10.970
Holland, the human body is a wondrous thing.

01:39:10.970 --> 01:39:16.130
Your and Talho's baby is developing at
a rate no different from any other human.

01:39:17.280 --> 01:39:20.850
Its development is completely unaffected
by the mother's own growth rate.

01:39:21.150 --> 01:39:25.290
When it's born, it won't be any
different from normal humans.

01:39:25.290 --> 01:39:26.620
You're kidding...

01:39:26.620 --> 01:39:28.410
That means our curse...

01:39:28.410 --> 01:39:30.860
...won't be passed down.

01:39:31.120 --> 01:39:32.890
Doggie... Ken-Goh...

01:39:32.890 --> 01:39:35.620
We heard the whole story from Talho.

01:39:35.620 --> 01:39:38.580
But you up and bolted, man!

01:39:38.580 --> 01:39:41.730
You even took a Super Pack with you.

01:39:41.730 --> 01:39:43.000
Guys...

01:39:43.360 --> 01:39:47.320
If we're gonna get to see your kid's face,
I'd say this world isn't so bad.

01:39:47.950 --> 01:39:49.900
Nope. Not so bad at all.

01:39:50.750 --> 01:39:53.010
--Holland.
- -Yeah?

01:39:53.270 --> 01:39:55.660
I want to show it everything.

01:39:55.660 --> 01:40:00.700
I want to show it the world that
its mom and dad lived their lives in.

01:40:02.500 --> 01:40:03.820
Me too.

01:40:06.330 --> 01:40:11.490
You know... The thing is, there really
is a place that I want to go.

01:40:11.660 --> 01:40:13.140
Do you know where it is?

01:40:13.900 --> 01:40:19.240
The thing is, to tell you truth, I always
wanted to go home to Warsaw.

01:40:20.040 --> 01:40:23.780
I know that this world
is full of fear and hate.

01:40:24.590 --> 01:40:28.000
I know that I'll suffer in this world.

01:40:28.000 --> 01:40:31.260
But you know what?
I realized that I didn't mind.

01:40:32.160 --> 01:40:37.700
Even if I'm locked up in a dark hospital
room and can only go out at night.

01:40:38.480 --> 01:40:41.740
Even if I lived out the
rest of my days like that.

01:40:42.660 --> 01:40:45.700
Because I have you there, Renton.

01:40:45.700 --> 01:40:50.020
The city where I met you
and spent my days with you...

01:40:50.590 --> 01:40:52.190
That's my fondest memory.

01:40:53.040 --> 01:40:55.040
My precious memory.

01:40:56.330 --> 01:40:59.230
But I don't mind if I lose that, not anymore.

01:41:00.330 --> 01:41:03.580
If that memory will inspire the EIZO...

01:41:03.580 --> 01:41:06.060
If it will let you survive,

01:41:06.700 --> 01:41:08.970
then I don't mind losing what makes me me.

01:41:09.750 --> 01:41:13.660
Because if you survive and keep on dreaming,

01:41:13.660 --> 01:41:16.870
then I'll still exist in your dreams.

01:41:16.870 --> 01:41:18.560
That's my dream.

01:41:19.930 --> 01:41:23.010
Goodbye, Renton. I love you.

01:41:23.410 --> 01:41:25.360
I'll see you in your dreams.

01:41:27.080 --> 01:41:30.200
Okay. Let's go, Nirvash.

01:41:35.250 --> 01:41:38.410
Hammer of God, energy discharge confirmed!

01:41:38.410 --> 01:41:39.920
Primary mechanism shows all green!

01:41:40.280 --> 01:41:44.490
No obstacles detected along
projected path, Corridor 999!

01:41:45.160 --> 01:41:49.580
No reaction in EIZO core!
T-minus 27 seconds to beam impact!

01:41:51.250 --> 01:41:55.840
Unknown object detected on
Corridor 999! Speed: Mach... 22!

01:41:55.840 --> 01:41:57.920
It's pursuing the beam at high speed!

01:41:57.920 --> 01:42:00.010
Wha--? That's impossible!

01:42:14.620 --> 01:42:18.790
Success! Hammer of God has scored
a direct hit on the EIZO core!

01:42:18.790 --> 01:42:21.120
Observation teams, we need situation reports!

01:42:21.120 --> 01:42:23.580
Well done, everyone.

01:42:23.580 --> 01:42:25.790
And now, the survivors will--

01:42:25.790 --> 01:42:27.620
Wait, what's that?!

01:42:32.910 --> 01:42:37.290
Come on, don't run so fast!

01:42:47.160 --> 01:42:49.330
What're ya doing, sis?

01:42:49.330 --> 01:42:51.560
I'm making a wish on the star.

01:42:51.560 --> 01:42:55.000
I'm wishing for a peaceful
world to come soon.

01:42:55.000 --> 01:42:56.730
--Me too!
- -Me too!

01:43:01.160 --> 01:43:04.720
Not to worry; peace will come soon enough.

01:43:05.430 --> 01:43:09.250
So long as we all keep dreaming of that day.

01:43:38.200 --> 01:43:41.950
Storms and waves that are off the scale
are emanating from the EIZO core!

01:43:41.950 --> 01:43:43.580
The world is being inundated!

01:43:43.580 --> 01:43:46.200
If this is God's reply...

01:43:46.200 --> 01:43:50.200
...it means we are no match for
powers beyond our understanding,

01:43:50.200 --> 01:43:52.710
no matter how mightily we struggle.

01:43:53.420 --> 01:43:57.960
Still, this spectacle...
Did you predict this?

01:43:58.570 --> 01:44:01.080
Coda, are you out there?

01:44:02.830 --> 01:44:04.610
Life is but a dream.

01:44:04.610 --> 01:44:05.590
A dream?

01:44:05.620 --> 01:44:11.770
Yes. All intelligent lifeforms
must dream in order to evolve.

01:44:12.250 --> 01:44:15.950
Say, do you know what you
need in order to dream?

01:44:15.950 --> 01:44:19.110
How philosophical of you... I don't know.

01:44:19.410 --> 01:44:22.250
In order to dream, you have to have memories.

01:44:22.250 --> 01:44:25.110
That's something that we EIZO lack.

01:44:26.250 --> 01:44:31.250
On this world, dreams are created by the
genetic information that all life possesses.

01:44:31.250 --> 01:44:34.410
The memories of the past that
you all carry around with you.

01:44:34.410 --> 01:44:37.470
Those memories are what you EIZO wanted?

01:44:38.350 --> 01:44:39.460
To what end?

01:44:39.830 --> 01:44:42.040
To fuse with humanity?

01:44:42.040 --> 01:44:43.310
Beats me.

01:44:43.660 --> 01:44:46.660
I'm just a simple observer.

01:44:46.660 --> 01:44:49.060
I'm not in a position to know such things.

01:44:49.500 --> 01:44:50.500
Ah.

01:44:50.500 --> 01:44:53.110
But I <i>will </i>know someday!

01:44:53.990 --> 01:44:57.620
When my people, who have
become one with this world,

01:44:57.620 --> 01:45:00.510
return from across that vast sea.

01:45:01.170 --> 01:45:06.660
When all life on this world has become
the stuff of myths, that's when I'll know.

01:45:07.790 --> 01:45:09.790
That will take a great deal of patience.

01:45:11.790 --> 01:45:19.040
Say, where do you suppose those children
I was chasing are watching all this?

01:45:33.660 --> 01:45:35.260
It's the new myth.

01:45:36.450 --> 01:45:38.450
It's the new myth...

01:45:38.450 --> 01:45:40.020
That we've all been wanting.

01:45:40.200 --> 01:45:42.330
I love you, Dominic!

01:45:42.330 --> 01:45:44.490
Now we can be together forever.

01:45:55.540 --> 01:45:58.720
Oh, come on. The pages are all blank.

01:45:59.620 --> 01:46:02.960
Pushy girl... Your way of telling
me to fill them in, I take it?

01:46:03.500 --> 01:46:05.880
All right, fine. I accept the challenge.

01:46:06.950 --> 01:46:10.330
It's what I ought to do, since I'm here.

01:46:10.330 --> 01:46:12.880
No, it's something that only I can do.

01:46:13.540 --> 01:46:19.680
Setting down what transpired here is a
fitting way to spend the rest of my years.

01:46:20.860 --> 01:46:24.930
So that my words will become
this world's myths one day.

01:46:25.330 --> 01:46:30.210
So that the new myth will
provide hope for the future.

01:46:59.120 --> 01:47:00.240
Where am I...?

01:47:03.700 --> 01:47:05.910
Eureka! What are you--

01:47:07.370 --> 01:47:08.610
W-Wait, I--

01:47:19.790 --> 01:47:21.290
Eureka...

01:47:23.580 --> 01:47:27.910
I don't believe it... It can't be...
Why did you do it?!

01:47:28.300 --> 01:47:29.320
Eureka!

01:47:35.910 --> 01:47:37.580
Nirvash!

01:47:39.330 --> 01:47:41.800
Nirvash, you're...

01:47:47.910 --> 01:47:51.740
Oh, I see. So that's what happened, Nirvash.

01:47:52.910 --> 01:47:55.450
We're back, aren't we?

01:47:56.950 --> 01:48:00.290
Yeah, I can tell. This is Warsaw, isn't it?

01:48:00.290 --> 01:48:06.330
This place that you brought us back to--
this is our Neverland, isn't it?

